2 CONT Exile and life to the Court [ change | modify the code ] In his homeland of Saint-Fargeau , from 1652 to 1657 , she started writing memories she continues writing at Chateau d'Eu in Normandy . In this story she recounts her memori
2 CONC es as a poignant confession. It paints a portrait says without false modesty his moods and even with some talent, tinted egotism. Still read today, his memoirs are an important testimony and, after all, one of a woman's life in xv
2 CONC ii th century , a prisoner of his education and his rank: where other memoirs say what they lived, she said what she felt.
2 CONT
2 CONT She much preferred the arts during his exile uncovering including Lully , who became a famous composer.
