1 NOTE Esmé Stuart, 1st Duke of Lennox was the son of John Stuart, 5th Seigneur d'Aubigny and Anne de la Queuille.1 He was born circa 1542.2 He married Catherine de Balsac, daughter of Guillaume de Balsac, Seigneur d'Entragues et Marcous
2 CONC sins and Louise d'es, circa 1572. He died on 26 May 1583 at Paris, France.1 He gained the title of Earl of Darnley. He succeeded to the title of 6th Seigneur d'Aubigny, de Berry [France, 1423] on 31 March 1567.1 In September 1579 
2 CONC he went to Scotland, after being brop in France.1 He was created 1st Earl of Lennox [Scotland] on 5 March 1579/80.1 He was created 1st Duke of Lennox [Scotland] on 5 August 1581.1
