1 NAME Dame Marie de Brizay Montbazilhac
2 GIVN Dame Marie de Brizay Montbazilhac
1 NAME Dame Marie de Brizay Montbazilhac
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Inligting:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.desbrisay.ca/DesBrisay6.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: "The family of "de Brisay" or Desbrisay, as it was at one time called, now existing in England, is without doubt of Huguenot descent, their common ancestor having been a Théophile de la Cour de Brisay, an officer in
2 CONC  the Regiment of Frédéric Guillaume Comté de Marton afterward, Earl of Lifford, 4th Son of the Comté de Roye, which Regiment was originally raised by Capitaine Théophile desBrisay. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  We may presume that this "Capitaine Théophile desBrisay", whose name we find in a "List of the Staff and Standing Officers of the Earl of Lifford's Regiment of Foot" in the year 1698, & who crossed over from Holland with the Fren
2 CONC ch Huguenot Regiments was a descendant of Pierre de Brisay III Chevalier and Seigneur de Denonville and Jacqueline D'Orleans Longueville his wife (see part 1st p.61.)
2 CONT  This Pierre de Brisay was one of the first, (though an Abbé of the Romish Church) to embrace the Reformed Faith.
2 CONT  His Son Jacques de Brisay, Chevalier and Siegneur de Denonville who was born at Denonville in 1579 (see part 1st p.35) fled to Holland and died at Heusden in 1625 leaving, by his wife Judith D'Argenson, a Son, Pierre de Brisay IV
2 CONC , and it is more than probable that other children were also born to Jacques de Brisay during his exile in Holland. Pierre de Brisay abjured the Reformed Faith and on his return to France succeeded to his Father's Estates, he alon
2 CONC e is mentioned by the French Genealogists.
2 CONT  This Pierre de Brisay, the welcome apostate, was created a Vicomté de Montbazillac, and Marquis d'Avesnes &ca.; he enjoyed many favors and dignities at the Court of France. Of his fourteen Children by his wife Louise d'Alés, nine
2 CONC  of them subsequently held high positions and preferments at the Same Court; we may therefore conclude, that they adhered to the original faith of their forefathers and were all Roman Catholics.
2 CONT  Presuming therefore, that there were other children born to Jacques de Brisay who settled and died in Holland cir. 1625 and that they, with their Father continued Huguenots & exiles from France, the descendant from one of the Son
2 CONC s, was most probably the Father of the Théophile de la Cour de Brisay of the Earl of Lifford's, French Huguenot Regiment, whose commission, we find, is dated in 1689, four years after the Revocation of the Edict of Nantes and 64 y
2 CONC ears after the death at Heusden in Holland of the Refugee Jacques de Brisay; who may have been his Grandfather (see part 1st page 35)
2 CONT
2 CONT Also: Archives of the Chamber of Accounts / Languedoc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hommage de Francois de Lambertie chevalier, Sr. of the place of Lambertie, Montbrun, Meslet, Puissabe, La Robiniere, Giral and other places for the reason of the fief, land and seigniory of Giral located in the parish of St Michel
2 CONC  in Angoumois, May 10, 1647 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Hommage de Pierre de Brisay knight sgr of the land, jurisdiction and viscount of Montbazilhac located in the seneschaussée of Perigueux coming from the Duchy of Guienne and crown of France, belonging to him by means of the donatio
2 CONC n given to him by dame Marie of Brisay Montbazilhac, widow of Mother Louis Bouchard d'Aubaterre living knight sgr de Montbazilhac, his paternal aunt. 9 August 1662- Ingestuur Ds.MG Muller
