1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on John Gordon:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p11531.htm#i115305
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gordon, 1st and last Viscount Melgum and Lord Aboyne [1]
2 CONT *M, #115305, 
2 CONT *d. 9 October 1630
2 CONT *Last Edited=26 Jan 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.49%
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gordon, 1st and last Viscount Melgum and Lord Aboyne was the son of George Gordon, 1st Marquess of Huntly and Lady Henrietta Stuart.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Sophia Hay, daughter of Francis Hay, 9th Earl of Erroll and Elizabeth Douglas, in 1626.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 9 October 1630 at Frendraugh Tower, Scotland, in a fire, without male issue.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Viscount Melgum and Lord Aboyne [Scotland] on 20 October 1627.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT On his death, his title became extinct.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of John Gordon, 1st and last Viscount Melgum and Lord Aboyne and Lady Sophia Hay
2 CONT *1. Hon. Henrietta Gordon3
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 52. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1336. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S323] Sir James Balfour Paul, The Scots Peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's The Peerage of Scotland (Edinburgh, Scotland: David Douglas, 1904), volume IX, page 6. Hereinafter cited as The Scots Peerage.
