1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lord Bernard Stewart is on the right in the profile photo (his brother, Lord John Stewart, is on the left) [painting by by Sir Anthony van Dyck]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Bernard_Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Bernard Stewart (1623 – 26 September 1645) was a Scottish aristocrat who served as a Royalist commander in the English Civil War. He was the youngest of five sons of Esmé Stewart, 3rd Duke of Lennox and his wife Katherine Cli
2 CONC fton, 2nd Baroness Clifton, and the brother of James Stewart, 1st Duke of Richmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Bernard was to be created Earl of Lichfield by King Charles I for his actions at the battles of Newbury and Naseby but died of injuries received leading a sortie against besieging Parliamentary forces in the Battle of Rowton 
2 CONC Heath in September 1645, before the patent could be implemented. The titles of Baron Newbury and Earl of Lichfield were instead created in December 1645 for his six-year-old nephew, Charles Stewart (1639–1672), the son of Bernard'
2 CONC s elder brother George Stewart, 9th Seigneur d'Aubigny, who had been killed at the Battle of Edgehill in 1642. His brother John was also killed in the war.
