2 CONT
2 CONT Henrietta Seton formerly Gordon aka Stewart Born 19 Oct 1621 in Scotlandmap ANCESTORS ancestors Daughter of George Gordon KB and Anne (Campbell) Gordon Sister of Jean (Gordon) Hamilton, George Gordon, Ann (Gordon) Drummond, Lewis 
2 CONC Gordon, James Gordon, Henry Gordon, Catherine Gordon, Charles Gordon 1st and Mary Gordon Wife of George Seton — married 19 Oct 1639 in Scotlandmap Wife of John Stewart — married 1649 (to 1651) in Scotlandmap DESCENDANTS descendant
2 CONC s Mother of George Seton Died 1651 in Scotlandmap
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Henrietta Gordon was the daughter of George Gordon, 2nd Marquess of Huntly and Lady Anne Campbell.1,2
2 CONT
2 CONT She married by contract, firstly, George Seton, Lord Seton, son of George Seton, 3rd Earl of Winton and Lady Anne Hay, on 19 October 1639.1
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, John Stewart, 2nd Earl of Traquair, son of John Stewart, 1st Earl of Traquair and Lady Catherine Carnegie, in 1649.1
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in June 1651 at Traquair, Peebles-shire, Scotland, in childbirth. no issue by him.3
2 CONT
2 CONT From 19 October 1639, her married name became Seton. From 1649, her married name became Stewart.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources THE PEERAGE 21475 Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1280. Charles Mosle
2 CONC y, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2013. Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 3, page 3928 http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/gg/gordon02.php
