1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LUDOVIC GRANT OF THAT ILK (aka LEWIS GRANT OF THAT ILK)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Holyrood Burial Register===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19th November, 1716. — Sir Ludovick Grant, of that ilk, was buried in the Church of Holyroodhouse, and lyes in the north-west corner of the church four foots from the north wall. The head of his coffin lyes below the north-west
2 CONC  window, and the foot of his coffin four foot from the wall upon the west side of the north door, the foot of his coffin being exactly where the head of his father's were laid upon the 10th of October 1663. [https://archive.org/de
2 CONC tails/scottishrecordso14scotuoft/page/6/mode/1up Holyrood Burial Register: 7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22nd August, 1719. — Sir Alexander Grant, of that ilk, was buried in the Church of Holyroodhouse upon the above- named Sir Ludovick Grant, his father's right hand, lying as above. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso14
2 CONC scotuoft/page/6/mode/1up Holyrood Burial Register: 7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
