2 CONT Laird Ludovic Grant, 8th of Freuchie and 1st of Grant
2 CONT Also Known As: ""The Highland King""
2 CONT Birthdate: 1641
2 CONT Birthplace: Frenchie, Perth, Scotland
2 CONT Death: before November 19, 1716
2 CONT Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland (United Kingdom)
2 CONT Place of Burial: Canongate, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland
2 CONT Immediate Family:
2 CONT Son of James Grant, 7th of Freuchie and Mary Stewart
2 CONT Husband of Janet Grant and Jean Houston
2 CONT Father of John Grant; Sir James Grant of that Ilk, 6th Baronet of Colquhoun; Brigadier-General Alexander Grant of that Ilk; Major George Grant of Culbin, Governor of Inverness Castle; Col. Lewis Grant of Dunphail and 9 others
2 CONT Brother of Margaret Mackenzie; Patrick Grant of Wester Elchies; Anne Grant and Mary Grant
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Ludovic-Grant-8th-of-Freuchie-and-1st-of-Grant/6000000002115890838
2 CONT ∼
2 CONT Sir Ludovick Grant was the 8th Earl of Freuchie and the 1st Earl of Grant. He was the son of James Grant, 7th of Freuchie and Lady Mary Stuart.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Janet Brodie, daughter of Alexander Brodie, 2nd of Lethen and Elizabeth Craig, on 16 or 20 December 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Between them having six sons and five daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Grant
2 CONT Brig.-Gen. Alexander Grant, 2nd of Grant, b. 1672, d. 14 Aug 1719
2 CONT Sir James Grant of Grant, 6th Bt.
2 CONT Major George Grant, d. Dec 1755
2 CONT Colonel Lewis Grant, d. 11 Mar 1742
2 CONT David Grant, b. 29 January 1693. No known marriage. d. Unknown
2 CONT Anne Grant m. Colonel William Grant, 1st of Ballindaloch
2 CONT Janet Grant, d. 10 Feb 1761, m. Roderick Mackenzie of Scatwell, 2nd Bt
2 CONT Margaret Grant, d. 1729, m. Simon "the Fox" Fraser Eleventh Lord Lovat
2 CONT Elizabeth Grant, m. Hugh (Rose) Rose XVIth of Kilravock
2 CONT Mary Grant, b. 17 March 1691 d. 31 December 1691.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married secondly on the 1st of March 1701, by contract Jean Houstoun (died 31 Jan 1734), daughter of Sir Patrick Houstoun of Houstoun, Bt, and widow of (a) Walter, 3rd son of Walter Dundas of Dundas, and (b) Richard Lockhart of
2 CONC  Lee (qv).
2 CONT He died and was buried on the 19th of November 1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Interred 19 Nov 1716 - lyes in the northwest corner of the church four foot from the north wall. The head of his coffin lyes below the northwest window, and the foot of his coffin four feet dfrom the wall upon the west side of the
2 CONC  north door.
2 CONT
