4 CONT
4 CONT He married, firstly, Lady Mary Montgomerie, daughter of Hugh Montgomerie, 7th Earl of Eglinton and Lady Mary Leslie, on 4 September 1662. [1] 
4 CONT
4 CONT He married, secondly, Christian Hepburn, daughter of John Hepburn of Adinstoun, before 6 March 1682. [1] 
4 CONT
4 CONT He succeeded to the title of 9th Lord Seton and to the title of 4th Earl of Winton in December 1650. [1] He was joint-commander of the the men of East Lothian at Pentland in 1666. [1] 
4 CONT
4 CONT He was Privy Councillor [Scotland] from 1674/5 to 1689 and Grand Master of the Scottish Household 1685.[2] 
4 CONT
4 CONT He received a novadamus, (regrant) on 31 Jul 1686 of his titles with remainder to the heirs male of his body, failing which to any he should nominate with like remainder, and, failing such nomination, to his heirs male, failing wh
4 CONC om to his nearest heirs and assigns, the eldest daughter always succeeding without division. [2][1] 
4 CONT
4 CONT He died on 6 March 1704 at age 61. [1] [3] 
