1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Additional Curator's Notes:===
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was the wife of Edward Johnston of New Kent, Virginia. Her parents are widely disputed, as is her date of birth. Her name is recorded simply as "Elizabeth" on the baptismal records of her first four children. Many believ
2 CONC e that her birth name was Walker. Her parents are variously given as Samuel Walker and Ann Keith, as Alexander Walker of Old Machar, as Alexander and Frances Walker of James City County, Virginia  and as William Johnson and Barbar
2 CONC a Forbes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth did marry Edward Johnson or Johnston c.1676. Edward's parentage is equally shaky. While most sources place him in the family of Dr. Arthur Johnston, there is only circumstantial proof that the son of Dr. Johnston named E
2 CONC dward was Edward Johnston of New Kent. DNA studies are underway but descendants have not been found.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please refer to http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~lksstarr/JohnsonSection/wlkcon.txt for an in-depth discussion about the parentage of Elizabeth who married Edward Johnston of New Kent. This source - http://kinnexions.com/sm
2 CONC lawson/walker.htm#AWalker - also points out lack of proof in several theories about this family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Edmonds-Zediker, Volunteer Curator, Jan. 5, 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT  ==================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT ? Elizabeth - b. Jan. 13, 1658; d. 1725, New Kent Co., VA. Virtually every detail of the family of Elizabeth WALKER and Edward JOHNSON/JONSTON is based on conjecture, including the names of their parents and children, reported by
2 CONT
2 CONT http://kinnexions.com/smlawson/walker.htm
2 CONT
