2 CONC ont-size: 14px;">His parents were the army officer&nbsp;<a class="new" style="text-decoration: none; color: #a55858; background: none;" title="George Keith, 8th Earl Marischal (page does not exist)" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/
2 CONC w/index.php?title=George_Keith,_8th_Earl_Marischal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1">George Keith, 8th Earl Marischal</a>&nbsp;(d. 1694) and the courtier Lady Mary Hay (d. 1701), third daughter of the&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: 
2 CONC none; color: #0b0080; background: none;" title="George Hay, 2nd Earl of Kinnoull" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Hay,_2nd_Earl_of_Kinnoull">2nd Earl of Kinnoull</a>. Keith succeeded to the earldom in March 1694, swore 
2 CONC loyalty to the&nbsp;<em>de facto</em>&nbsp;monarchy, took up his seat in Scotland's parliament in July 1698, was sworn into the privy council in June 1701 and made a&nbsp;<a class="mw-redirect" style="text-decoration: none; color:
2 CONC  #0b0080; background: none;" title="Knight of the Thistle" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knight_of_the_Thistle">knight of the Thistle</a>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background: none;" title
2 CONC ="James Francis Edward Stuart" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Francis_Edward_Stuart">James Francis Edward Stuart</a>&nbsp;in 1705. However, he was imprisoned in&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; back
2 CONC ground: none;" title="Edinburgh Castle" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edinburgh_Castle">Edinburgh Castle</a>&nbsp;for Jacobitism during the 1708 rising then sent to London for trial once it was over, but still managed to be 
2 CONC made one of 16&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background: none;" title="Representative peer" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Representative_peer">representative peers</a>&nbsp;at Westminster from 1710 to
2 CONC  1712. He was anti-<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background: none;" title="Treaty of Union" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Union">Union</a>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0
2 CONC b0080; background: none;" title="Tory" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tory">Tory</a>&nbsp;in political sympathies and founded a medicine chair at&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background: none;" title=
2 CONC "Marischal College" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marischal_College">Marischal College</a>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<a style="text-decoration: none; color: #0b0080; background: none;" title="Aberdeen" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki
2 CONC /Aberdeen">Aberdeen</a>&nbsp;(though he did not endow it). John Macky described him as:</p> <table class="cquote" style="font-size: 14px; color: #252525; font-family: sans-serif; background-color: transparent; margin: auto; border
2 CONC -collapse: collapse; border: none; width: auto;"> <tbody> <tr> <tdstyle="width: 20px; vertical-align: top; border: none; color: #b2b7f2; font-size: 40px; font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-weight: bold; line-height
2 CONC : 0.6em; padding: 10px;">&ldquo;</td> <td style="vertical-align: top; border: none; padding: 4px 10px;">very wild, inconstant and passionate; does everything by starts; hath abundance of flashy wit, and by reason of his quality, h
2 CONC ath good interest in the country; all Courts endeavour to have him at their side for he gives himself liberty of talking when he is not pleased with the Government. He is a thorough Libertine, yet sets up mightily for Episcopy; a 
2 CONC hard drinker; a thin body; a middle stature; ambitious of popularity.<sup id="cite_ref-1" class="reference" style="line-height: 1; unicode-bidi: isolate; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 11.2px;"><a style="text-decoration: none; co
