1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET MONTGOMERIE (aka MARGARET MONNTGOMRY)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Montgomerie is the first child and eldest daughter of Hugh Montgomerie, Earl of Eglinton, and his second wife Mary Leslie. She was born before 15 December 1636, the date upon which her baptism was registered at Leslie 
2 CONC in Fife, Scotland. Her baptismal Record reads as follows: "Hugh Lord Monntgomry had ane daur baptized Margaret procreat bee his wyffe La : Marie Leslie C : off Eglingtoun witnesss Lord Johne [ . . . . .   ] my Lord Lindsay my Lord
2 CONC  Rothes and sundrie uthers". [National Records of Scotland, Leslie Baptisms, 1600-1645, reference OPR.444/6] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076325082889& Image of Baptismal Record]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Montgomerie married James Campbell, second Earl of Louden. According to Sir James Balfour Paul, they were married after 25 November  1666 "when she accepted him". [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05paul#page
2 CONC /507/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, V, p. 507]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 September [16]66: Letter from the Earl of Loudoun to Lady Margaret Montgomerie. 'The continuance of my misfortune in not being yett in a conditione to wait upon your ladyship is beyond expression vexing..' Dated [16]66. [Misc
2 CONC ellaneous papers formerly belonging to Mrs. Drummond Forbes, Millearne, Auchterarder. Documents contained in folder marked 'Old letters and papers and copies of old letters for Charles H. Drummond'.] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.g
2 CONC ov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f479%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomerie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1636&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earl of Angus documents, literary letters, reference GD1
2 CONC /479/4]'''
