1 NOTE {geni:about_me} King Louis I of Spain (Spanish: Luis, August 25, 1707 – August 31, 1724), born Louis-Philippe of Spain, was the eldest son of Philip V of Spain by his first Queen consort, Maria Louisa of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 20 January 1722 he married Louise Elisabeth of Orléans (1709–1742), a daughter of Philippe II, Duc d'Orléans. She did not fit into the religious Spanish court well and she often refused to speak to her husband. There were no ch
2 CONC ildren of the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis ruled for a short period between the time his father Philip V abdicated in his favour (15 January 1724) and his death from smallpox, just over 7 months later. On his death his father returned to the throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT The only coins minted in Mexico during his reign never reached Spain as the ship containing them was wrecked in the Caribbean. An expedition to recover them is under way.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Luis I de Borbón, Rey de España
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #105785, b. 25 August 1707, d. 31 August 1724
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=4 Mar 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=8.8%
2 CONT
2 CONT      Luis I de Borbón, Rey de España was born on 25 August 1707 at Madrid, Spain. (1) He was the son of Felipe V de Borbón, Rey de España and Maria Luisa Gabriela di Savoia. He married Louise Elizabeth d'Orléans, daughter of Phili
2 CONC ppe II d'Orléans, Duc d'Orléans and Françoise Marie de Bourbon, on 20 January 1722 at Lerma, Spain.1 He died on 31 August 1724 at age 17 at Madrid, Spain. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Luis I de Borbón, Rey de España was a member of the House of Bourbon. He succeeded to the title of Rey Luis I de España in 1724.
2 CONT
