2 CONT * '''Details''': [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Campbell,_1st_Duke_of_Argyll]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Archibald Campbell, 1st Duke of Argyll & 10th Earl of Argyll'''
2 CONT ==
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest son of Archibald Campbell, 9th Earl of Argyll and Mary Stuart, daughter of James Stuart, 4th Earl of Moray, Campbell sought to recover his father's estates (by gaining King James VII's favour). However, after failing to
2 CONC  do so, he supported William and Mary's quest for the throne; this important support led to the monarchs returning his father's estate. Also, he was made a Privy Councillor. He was William's chief Scottish advisor, and was colonel
2 CONC -in-chief of the Earl of Argyll's Regiment of Foot, that was involved in the 1692 massacre of the MacDonalds of Glen Coe, but took no part in any of its field operations. He was made a duke in 1701.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 12 March 1678, he married Elizabeth Tollemache (daughter of Elizabeth and Sir Lionel Tollemache, 3rd Baronet at Edinburgh, Scotland. Elizabeth's stepfather John Maitland, 1st Duke of Lauderdale was a dominant figure in Scottish
2 CONC  politics of the era. They had four children, born at Ham House outside London:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Campbell, 2nd Duke of Argyll (10 October 1680 – 4 October 1743)
2 CONT # Archibald Campbell, 3rd Duke of Argyll (June 1682 – 15 April 1761)
2 CONT # Lady Anne Campbell (born before 1686 – 20 October 1736), m. James Stuart, 2nd Earl of Bute
2 CONT # Lady Margaret Campbell (2 June 1690 – 1742), m. Colonel Michael Marion Woods
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1st Duke of Argyll is buried at Kilmun Parish Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References''' Stephen, Leslie, ed. (1886). "Campbell, Archibald (d.1703)" . Dictionary of National Biography. 8. London: Smith, Elder & Co. Lundy, Darryl. "Archibald Campbell, 1st Duke of Argyll". The Peerage.[unreliable source
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia - [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Campbell,_1st_Duke_of_Argyll]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Archibald was one of those offered the Crown of the Prince of Orange, and on 23 Jun 1701, he was created Duke of Argyll, Marquis of Kintyre and Lorn, Earl of Campbell and Cowal, Viscount of Lochow and Glenila, Lord of Inveruray, M
2 CONC ull, Morven and Tiree, with remainder to his heirs male whatever.  In 1689 he offered to raise a regiment of six hundred foot, which was accepted by the Estates, and he received command of this body, which was called the Earl of A
2 CONC rgyll's Regiment of Foot.
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald Campbell was featured in the Bear Grylls Who Do You Think You Are ...skip to the last part to view
2 CONT https://www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer/episode/m001mx00/who-do-you-think-you-are-series-20-4-bear-grylls
