1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JAMES GRANT OF THAT ILK Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''formerly James Grant of Pluscarden; afterwards Sir James Grant Colquhoun of Luss, Baronet'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir James Colquhoun</strong>, subsequently (after 1719) <strong>Grant, Baronet [S 1625]</strong>, formerly James Grant of Pluscardine, 2nd son of Ludovic Grant, of Grant (died 1717), by his 1st wife, Janet, daughter and h
2 CONC eir, of Alexander Brodie of Lethen. He was born 28 July 1679, and, having married 29 January 1702, Anne (born 1665), only child of Sir Humphrey Colquhoun, the last Baronet, by Margaret his wife, succeeded to the Baronetcy on the d
2 CONC eath of his said father-in-law, in 1718 (by virtue of the special rem. in the <em>novodamus</em> of that dignity), and to the estate of Luss, by virtue of the entail thereof, on which occassion he took the name of Colquhoun. The n
2 CONC ext year, however, he succeeded on the death, in 1719, s.p.s., of his elder brother, Brig.-Gen. Alexander Grant, to the paternal estate of Grant, and reassumed is patronymic of Grant. He was M.P. for Inverness-shire (three Parliam
2 CONC ents), 1722-41, and for the Elgin burghs, 1741-47. His wife died 25 June 1724, aged 39. He died 16 January 1746/7."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n313/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 295
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir James Grant of Grant, 6th Bt.''' was born on 28 July 1679.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Ludovic Grant, 8th of Freuchie and 1st of Grant and Janet Brodie.4,5 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anne Colquhoun, daughter of Sir Humphrey Colquhoun of Luss, 5th Bt. and Margaret Houstoun, on 29 January 1702.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 16 January 1747 at age 67.4
2 CONT
2 CONT On 30 August 1625 created ) under terms of a regrant to the latter of 1704.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was given the name of James Grant at birth.6 In 1718 OF GRANT later COLQUHOUN OF LUSS (on inheriting father-in-law's btcy (NS.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of  6th Baronet Colquhoun, of Luss [N.S., 1625] in 1718.4 In 1718 his name was legally changed to James Colquhoun.4 In 1719 his name was legally changed to James Grant.6
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir James Grant of Grant, 6th Bt. and Anne Colquhoun
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Anne Drummonda Grant7 d. 15 Feb 1771
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Penuel Grant7
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Clementina Grant+7 d. 1 Jun 1765
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Jean Grant+1 b. 28 Sep 1705, d. 16 Jan 1788
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.Sir Ludovick Grant of Grant, 7th Bt.+7 b. 13 Jan 1707, d. 18 Mar 1773
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.Sir James Colquhoun of Luss, 1st Bt.+7 b. 22 Feb 1714, d. 18 Nov 1786
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.Lt.-Gen. Francis Grant+7 b. 10 Aug 1717, d. 30 Dec 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.Captain Charles Grant7 b. 3 Apr 1723, d. 11 Feb 1772
2 CONT
