1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>William Forbes</strong>, born 1668, third son of Sir Thomas F. of Waterton, and grand-nephew to the first Earl of Aberdeen; studied medicine M.D. (Pisa); returned home and graduated at King's College M.A. (21st June 1694);
2 CONC  ord. to Leslie 30th April 1701 ; called 10th Feb., trans, and adm. 12th June 1706 ; died 21st Jan. 1738. He left 300 merks to the poor of the parish. He marr. Janet (born Jan. 1675, died 13th April 1736), daugh. of James Gregory,
2 CONC  Professor of Mathematics in Univ. of Edinburgh, inventor of the reflecting telescope, and had issue— 
2 CONT * James, physician, Aberdeen, born 4th Dec. 1701, died 19th July 1774 [his son William, a successful Aberdeen merchant, purchased the estate of Echt] ; 
2 CONT * John ; 
2 CONT * Thomas, born 4th Jan. 1704; 
2 CONT * Helen, born 29th Aug. 1705 (marr. John McInnes, min. of Logie-Colstone; 
2 CONT * George; 
2 CONT * William, born 1713, died 22nd April 1731 ; 
2 CONT * Julia ; 
2 CONT * Katherine (marr. Oct. 1730, William Dyce, school-master at Selkirk) ; 
2 CONT * Jean (marr. Andrew Moir, min. of Towie) ; 
2 CONT * Susanna (marr. James Johnston, min. of Crimond) ; 
2 CONT * Mary, born 1713, died 21st Nov. 1743; 
2 CONT * Margaret, died May 1769; Ann, died April 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc06scot#page/204/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VI, page 204
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * Gill of Savock, Andrew John Mitchell. [https://archive.org/stream/familiesofmoirby00gill#page/54/mode/2up The families of Moir and Byres]. Edinburgh : Scott & Ferguson, 1885. page 54
