2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 August 1690: Instrument of sasine in favour of Mungo Buchanan, writer in Edinburgh and Anna Barclay, his spouse, in a yearly annual rent of £48 Scots, or such an annual rent as should correspond to the principal sum of 1,200 
2 CONC merks Scots, to be uplifted and taken out of the lands of Hilltoun Mailler, lying within the Parish of Forteviot and Sheriffdom of Perth. Recorded in the General Register of Sasines 29 Sep 1690. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH8%2f216&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Mungo+Buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, reference RH8/216]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 November 1695: Tack by Mungo Buchanan, WS, and Anna Barclay, his spouse, to William Sympsone [Simpson], tenant in Hilltoun [Hilton], of half of the lands of Hilltoun Mailler [Hilton Mailor], parish of Forteviot, sheriffdom o
2 CONC f Perth, for 19 years, reserving the salmon fishing. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD82%2f372&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Mungo+Buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Makgill, Viscounts Oxfuird, reference GD82/372]'''
2 CONT
