2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 December 1724: Ante-Nuptial Marriage Contract between Hugh Fraser of Kinneries [Kinnaries] and Lady Margaret Leslie, daughter of deceased Patrick, Count Lesly of Balquhyn [Balquhain], whereby the said Margaret assigns him th
2 CONC e sum of 9000 merks Scots contained in bond by the deceased George Leslie of Balquhyne, her brother german, and said Hugh binds himself to infeft said Margaret in liferent in lands of Fannellan [Fanellan] and Kiltarlatie [Kiltarli
2 CONC ty] if she survived him with no children, and in an annualrent of £600 Scots from said lands if there were children. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD23%2f10%2f527&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=george+leslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1700&dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Additional Bught Papers presented by Major Duncan G. Warrand OBE on 20th July 1945., reference GD23/10/527]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/historicalrecord03lesluoft/historicalrecord03lesluoft/page/n4/mode/1up Historical Records of the Family of Leslie from 1067-1868-9 etc. By Colonel Leslie of Balquhain, KH., (Edmonston and Douglas, E
2 CONC dinburgh, 1869), 680 pp. including index]'''
