1 NOTE {geni:about_me} gravemarker reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Here lies Margaret Fairly
2 CONT
2 CONT Departed Life 20 Aug. 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT Aged LXII Years"
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/K2Y4-VHD FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 4 2021, 22:12:56 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Fairly/Fairley
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John Fairly (b. abt 1717 Scotland; d. 1798 NC). Margaret and John were married about 1747 in Argyllshire, Scotland. In 1770, John and Margaret, with their children, immigrated aboard the ship Edinburgh to Wilmington, North
2 CONC  Carolina. The family eventually settled along Drowning Creek (Lumber River) in what was then Richmond County, NC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT All the children of Margaret Stewart and John Fairly were born in Scotland. They were the parents at least seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald Fairley (1749-1807)
2 CONT Mary Fairley McEachin (1751-1834)
2 CONT Alexander Fairley (1753-1827)
2 CONT Daniel Fairley (1756-  )
2 CONT Robert Fairley (1760-1821)
2 CONT Ann Fairley McGill (1764-1795)
2 CONT John Fairley Jr.(1766-1854)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Records indicate that subsequent generations of the John & Margaret Stewart Fairly family spelled their surname with an "e" - "Fairley".
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/133518013/margaret-fairly Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 12 2023, 3:04:45 UTC''
