2 CONT "<strong>Edward, sixth titular Duke of Perth</strong>, and, but for the attainder, ninth Earl of Perth, who succeeded, was the half-brother of John, being the son of James, first titular Duke, by Mary, his third wife. He was born 
2 CONC in the Castle of Stirling in 1690, during the imprisonment of his parents there...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died s.p. in Paris, 6 February 1760, and was buried in the Parish Chapel of St Marguerite. He married, at St Germains, 25 November 1709, Elizabeth, eldest daughter of Charles, second Earl of Middleton."
2 CONT
