1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Gordon,_2nd_Duke_of_Gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT General Alexander Gordon, 2nd Duke of Gordon (c. 1678 – 28 November 1728), styled Earl of Enzie until 1684 and the Marquess of Huntly from 1684 to 1716, was a Scottish peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought with the Jacobites at the Battle of Sheriffmuir, with three hundred horsemen and two thousand foot. http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Sheriffmuir
2 CONT
2 CONT On 12 February 1716, he surrendered at Gordon Castle, to John Gordon, 16th Earl of Sutherland. He was imprisoned at Edinburgh, but obtained a pardon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Gordon was the son of George Gordon, 1st Duke of Gordon.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Henrietta Mordaunt (ca. 1688–1760), daughter of Charles Mordaunt, 3rd Earl of Peterborough, before 13 February 1707; they had children.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gordon-2880
2 CONT https://www.allabouthistory.co.uk//History/Scotland/Person/Alexander-Gordon-2nd-Duke-Gordon-1678-1728.html
2 CONT http://www.montyhistnotes.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I5075&tree=MontyHistNotes_II
2 CONT https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/Alexander_Gordon,_2nd_Duke_of_Gordon_(c1678-1728)
2 CONT https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Dictionary_of_National_Biography,_1885-1900/Gordon,_Alexander_(1678%3F-1728)
2 CONT https://www.scottish-places.info/people/famousfirst1076.html
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LCMP-WZ3/capt-thomas-gordon-1678-1762
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/133355947/alexander-gordon
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Duke of Gordon. Extensive biography on Wikipedia. Interred in aisle at Trinity Church, Elgin
2 CONT
2 CONT Caledonian Mercury - Thursday 28 November 1728, p 4:
2 CONT Edinburgh, Nov 28. On Friday morning last, about 1 o'clock, died at his seat of Gordon-castle, the most Noble and Illustrious ALEXANDER, Duke of Gordon, of a malignant Indisposition in his breast, attended with a shortness of brea
2 CONC th, which in 6 days carried off his Grace. A Prince, whom Heaven had blessed with Variety of uncommon endowments; if consummate Honour and Integrity, an extensive Charity, innate Love of Virtue, and a scrupulous aversion to whatev
2 CONC er vicious or irregular, all sweetened with a blest natural temper, be allow'd to pass for ought: And who, among the other shining Qualifications worthy of his high birth, was so fully Master of that Humility peculiar to his Illus
2 CONC trious Family, that he was justly esteem'd the most affable Man living. But as we cannot pretend in a News-paper sufficiently to do Justice to the Memory of so great and worthy a Prince, we shall briefly say, That he will be alway
2 CONC s justly regreted by good Men.
2 CONT His Grace has left issue, 4 sons and 7 daughters: Cosmos George, Marquis of Huntly, born April 27, 1720; Lord Charles, July 7th, 1721; Lord Lewis, December 22d 1724; Lord Adam, January 10th, 1728; Lady Henrietta born March 10th 17
2 CONC 08; Lady Mary, Febr 6th 1712; Lady Anne June 5th, 1713; Lady Elizabeth Febr 14, 1717; Lady Jean Jan 28, 1719; Lady Katherine Decr 2d 1723; Lady Charlotte, Sept 21, 1726. And her Grace is well gone with Child.
2 CONT We hear that his Grace was in the 48th or 49th Year of his Age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT JAMES HENRY
2 CONT Duke of Richmond & Gordon
2 CONT ALEXANDER, 2nd Duke
2 CONT Died 22nd Nov 1728 aged 42;
2 CONT COSMO GEORGE, 3rd Duke
2 CONT Died 5th August 1752 aged 32
2 CONT ALEXANDER, 4th Duke
2 CONT died 17th June 1728 aged 84;
2 CONT GEORGE, 5th & Last Duke
2 CONT Died 28th May 1836 aged 66.
