1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 66.  John Murray of Bowhill married Margaret Scott and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 83.  John16 Murray (John Murray of15 Bowhill, John14 Murray, Knight of Philiphaugh, James13, John Murray of12 Philiphaugh, Patrick Murray of11 Falahill, James Murray (the younger) of10, Patrick9 Murray, of Falahill, James8, John
2 CONC 7, Patrick Murray of6 Falahill, John Murray of Falahill &5 Philiphaugh, Patrick Murray of4 Falahill, Alexander3 de Moravia, Roger2, Archibald1) was born 04 Feb 1677 in Ensdale, Scotland, and died Feb 1728.  He married Anne Bennet 
2 CONC 29 Apr 1712, daughter of Archibald Bennet of Chesters.  She was born 16 Nov 1694, and died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for John Murray: John Murray of Unthank
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Letters of James Murray, Loyalist edited by Nina Moore Tiffany
2 CONT
2 CONT Ms. Tiffany writes;
2 CONT
2 CONT "Scattered at longer or shorter distances from Unthank, throughout the neighboring counties, were a score of Scottish households whose inmates were directly related to him (John Murray) or connected with him by marriage. Stewarts,
2 CONC  Grahams, Pringles, Murrays, Bennets, Kerrs, Scotts, and others had quarreled and married, thriven and multiplied, until the population had become one vast cousinship, bound together by that clannish loyalty which, quite apart fro
2 CONC m pride of name, is ineradicable in the Scots to the present day."
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Anne Bennet: Source: Letters of James Murray, Loyalist
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Bennet, daughter of the Laird of Chesters, was a cousin of John Murray of Unthank
2 CONT
2 CONT More About John Murray and Anne Bennet: Marriage: 29 Apr 1712
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Murray and Anne Bennet are:
2 CONT
2 CONT +     90             i.   James17 Murray, born 09 Aug 1713 in Unthank, Scotland; died 1781.
2 CONT
2 CONT        91            ii.   Archibald Murray, born 15 Apr 1715; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT        92           iii.   Barbara Murray, born 03 Feb 1717; died 1761.  She married Thomas Clark; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT        93           iv.   Anne Murray, born 23 Jan 1719; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT +     94            v.   Dr. John Murray, born 29 Nov 1721 in Unthank, Dumfriesshire, Scotland; died 26 Sep 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT        95           vi.   Andrew Murray, born 03 Jan 1723; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT        96           vii.   Capt. William Murray, born 10 Apr 1724; died 1784.  He married Elizabeth Jones 1781; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Capt. Murray and Elizabeth Jones: Marriage: 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT        97          viii.   Elizabeth Murray, born 07 Jul 1726; died Unknown.  She married (1) Thomas Campbell; died Unknown.  She married (2) James Smith; died Unknown.  She married (3) Ralph Inman; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Elizabeth Murray:
2 CONT
2 CONT Arrived in America in 1749 accompanied by brother James Murray, his wife and daughter Dorothy.  Their ship put in at Boston where Elizabeth remained and launched a modest but successful business career with the aid of her brother'
2 CONC s advice and credit with London merchants.  She first lived on King Street with Mrs. Barker, a motherly woman whose sisters and daughters became valued friends of the Murray family.  Dorothy later lived with Elizabeth.  In 1755 El
2 CONC izabeth married Thomas Campbell, a Scotch merchant and trader, and the son of James Campbell.  Thomas did not live very long after their marriage (date unknown).  She married James Smith in March, 1760.  James was around 70 years 
2 CONC of age when they married and was quite wealthy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for James Smith: James Smith a prosperous figure in Boston was a sugar baker, whose refinery had been working since 1729 or before.  He had amassed wealth and property.
2 CONT
2 CONT        98           ix.   Andrew Murray, born 10 Apr 1728; died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * http://www.murraysmithgenealogypage.bravehost.com/MURR.HTM
