1 TITL Lady
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lady Henrietta Johnstone''' was born on 11 November 1682 and died on 25 November 1750 at age 68. Her married name became Hope.
2 CONT
2 CONT Listen to a sample of the Scottish reel named after her here: [http://www.amazon.com/Lady-Harriet-Hopes-Reel-Mrs-Johnstones/dp/B004R76QRS Lady Harriot Hope's Reel] or on [http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0vXWicmRZbg YouTube], where 
2 CONC "Lady Hope's Reel"  was a track from the album "Birth of Liberty - Music of the American Revolution."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT * from [http://www.ibiblio.org/fiddlers/LADYG_LADYL.htm The Fiddler's Companion] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Harriet/Harriot Hope has been identified (by Jerry O’Sullivan & Brian McCandless) as Lady Henrietta Johnstone (1682-1750), married to the Charles Hope (1681-1742), 1st Earl of Hopetoun in 1699. Henrietta was the daughter of W
2 CONC illiam Johnstone, the first Marquess of Annandale, and bore the Earl thirteen children. One of their grandchildren was a highly decorated naval officer who fought in the Battle of Trafalgar. Charles Hope was a Member of Parliament
2 CONC  for Linlithgow in 1702, a Privy Councillor in 1702, and an Earl by 1703; he was a supporter of the Treaty of Union, wedding England and Scotland in 1707. Further titles followed. He was responsible for the erection of Hopetoun Ho
2 CONC use, designed by Sir William Bruce, a prominent period architect. Henrietta herself inherited the estates and titles of the Johnstone family upon the death of her brother, James Johnstone (who thereby disinherited their half-broth
2 CONC ers), but she held them only briefly before they went to another member of the family, George. Unfortunately, George (who never married), Marquess of Annandale, was declared legally insane in 1748, and Henrietta’s son, John Hope, 
2 CONC 2nd Earl of Hopetoun, was appointed ‘trustee in lunacy” for his half-uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents:  daughter of Sir William Johnstone, 1st Marquess of Annandale and Sophia Fairholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married
2 CONT #  Charles Hope, 1st Earl of Hopetoun, son of John Hope of Hopetoun and Lady Margaret Hamilton, on 31 August 1699.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Henrietta Johnstone and Charles Hope, 1st Earl of Hopetoun
2 CONT # Lady Sophia Hope4 b. 31 May 1702, d. 25 Apr 1761
2 CONT # John Hope, 2nd Earl of Hopetoun+2 b. 7 Sep 1704, d. 12 Feb 1781
2 CONT # Lady Henrietta Hope+4 b. 21 Feb 1706, d. 17 Feb 1745
2 CONT # Lady Margaret Hope b. 19 Dec 1708, d. 13 Jan 1778
2 CONT # Hon. Charles Hope-Vere+5 b. 8 May 1710, d. 30 Dec 1791
2 CONT # Lady Helen Hope+6 b. 27 Jul 1711, d. 26 Dec 1778
2 CONT # Lady Christian Hope6 b. 21 Mar 1714, d. 31 May 1799
2 CONT # Hon. William Hope6 b. 3 Jun 1715, d. 24 Nov 1715
2 CONT # Lady Anne Hope6 b. 22 Jul 1718, d. 24 Dec 1727
2 CONT # Lady Charlotte Hope b. 9 Mar 1720, d. 24 Nov 1788
2 CONT # Lady Rachel Hope6 b. 11 Jul 1721
