1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/113072069/james-johnstone
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd Marquess of Annandale
2 CONT
2 CONT James Johnstone, 3rd Earl of Annandale and Hartfell and 2nd Marquess of Annandale, was born about 1687-8 and was the eldest son of William Johnstone, 2nd Earl of Annandale and Hartfell and 1st Marquess of Annandale, by his first w
2 CONC ife Sophia Fairholm. He succeeded his father in 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT He spent most of his adult life traveling in Italy where he amassed a great collection of art and antiquities. In 1726 he attempted to legally prevent his half-brothers from inheriting his peerages and estates and directed that th
2 CONC ese should pass to his sister Henrietta Hope, Countess of Hopetoun, and her descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However, this attempt was only partly successful for, when he died in Italy in 1730 aged 42, only his Scottish lands and his art collection passed to Henrietta, while his peerages (which could not be lawfully alienated in the way 
2 CONC he intended) passed to his half-brother George who succeeded as 4th Earl of Annandale and Hartfell and 3rd Marquess of Annandale.
2 CONT
2 CONT His body was returned from Italy and buried in Westminster Abbey. His portrait hangs today at Hopetoun House near Edinburgh.
