1 NAME Gilbert /Johnstone/ Sr.
2 GIVN Gilbert
2 SURN Johnstone
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Johnstone
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Brompton Plantation, North Carolina
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1699
2 PLAC Annandale
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1775
2 PLAC Brompton Plantation, Elizabethtown, Bladen County, North Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Jacobite
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gilbert Johnstone, John’s second son, married to his Irish cousin Caroline Johnstone of Armagh, entertained his father sentiments, regarding the then rulers of Great Britain as usurpers.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert, third son of James Johnstone, 1st Earl of Annandale, left Scotland and went to Ireland in 1715.  He married there in 1724.  In 1745 Gilbert and his eldest son, Gilbert Johnstone Jr., joined the chevalier Charles Edward St
2 CONC uart and were at Culloden (1746), where the elder was wounded, but they escaped and with their family came to North Carolina in 1746, as exiles - outlaws.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Sr, died at "Brompton".
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: "Some Prominent Virginia Families" by Louise Pecquet du Bellet
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Gilbert Johnston fought at the Battle of Cullodon. He married Caroline Johnston and settled in Bladen, NC. Their children were: Gilbert, Henry, Caroline, Gabriel, Robert, William, Isabel and John."
2 CONT
2 CONT Wayne County NC Heritage Series - The Johnston Family Connection  The Mount Olive Tribune 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://files.usgwarchives.net/nc/wayne/heritage/johnston2.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert, third son of James Johnstone, 1st Earl of Annandale, left Scotland and went to Ireland in 1715. He married there in 1724. In 1745 Gilbert and his eldest son, Gilbert Johnstone Jr., joined the chevalier Charles Edward Stua
2 CONC rt and were at Culloden (1746), where the elder was wounded, but they escaped and with their family came to North Carolina in 1746, as exiles - outlaws.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Emigration''': 1746 - Moved to Cape Fear, North Carolina
2 CONT * '''Military service''': Wounded at the Battle of Culloden/
2 CONT * '''Residence''': United States
