1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jane Hamilton''' was born on 19 August 1726 at London, England. She died on 13 November 1771 at age 45 at St. Petersburg, Russia, from consumption. She was buried at Audley Street Chapel, St. George Hanover Squa
2 CONC re, London, England. From 24 July 1753, her married name became Cathcart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  daughter of Captain Hon. Archibald Hamilton and Lady Jane Hamilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # Lt.-Gen. Sir Charles Schaw Cathcart, 9th Lord Cathcart, son of Maj.-Gen. Charles Cathcart, 8th Lord Cathcart and Marion Shaw, on 24 July 1753 at Greenwich Hospital, Greenwich, London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Children of Jane Hamilton and Lt.-Gen. Sir Charles Schaw Cathcart, 9th Lord Cathcart include:
2 CONT # Hon. Jane Cathcart+5 b. 20 May 1754, d. 5 Dec 1790
2 CONT # General William Schaw Cathcart, 1st Earl Cathcart+6 b. 17 Sep 1755, d. 16 Jun 1843
2 CONT # Mary Cathcart6 b. 1757, d. 1792
2 CONT # Louisa Cathcart, Countess of Mansfield+6 b. c 1758, d. 11 Jul 1843
2 CONT # Colonel Hon. Charles Allan Cathcart6 b. 8 Dec 1759, d. 10 Jun 1788
2 CONT # Rev. Hon. Archibald Hamilton Cathcart+6 b. 25 Jul 1764, d. 10 Oct 1841
2 CONT
