1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note that WIkipedia's birthdate appears to be incorrect, according to The Peerage http://www.thepeerage.com/p10978.htm#i109778
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Hamilton_(diplomat)_ '''Sir William Hamilton''', KB, PC, FRS, FRSE] (13 December 1730 – 6 April 1803) was a British diplomat, politician, antiquarian and vulcanologist who served as the Envoy 
2 CONC Extraordinary to the Kingdom of Naples from 1764 to 1800. After sitting in the House of Commons of Great Britain from 1761 to 1764, he began working as a diplomat, succeeding Sir James Gray as the British ambassador to the Kingdom
2 CONC  of Naples. While in Italy, Hamilton became involved in studying local volcanoes and collecting antiquities, becoming a fellow of the Royal Society and being given the Copley Medal. His second wife was Emma Hamilton, who was famed
2 CONC  as the mistress of Horatio Nelson, 1st Viscount Nelson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT == Other References ==
