1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jane_Scott,_Countess_of_Dalkeith
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Scott, Countess of Dalkeith (24 May 1701 – 31 August 1729),[1] formerly Lady Jane Douglas, was the first wife of Francis Scott, 2nd Duke of Buccleuch, but died prior to his succeeding to the dukedom.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in London, the fourth daughter of James Douglas, 2nd Duke of Queensberry, and his wife, the former Mary Boyle, and thus a cousin of the future duke. The future duke, then Earl of Dalkeith, was to have been married to 
2 CONC her namesake Lady Jane Douglas, the daughter of James Douglas, 2nd Marquess of Douglas, but the Duchess of Queensberry is said to have stepped in to preempt this arrangement.
2 CONT
2 CONT They were married on 5 April 1720 at the Earl of Rochester's House, Privy Gardens, Whitehall.[2] Lady Jane died in 1729 at Langley, Buckinghamshire, and was buried at Dalkeith Castle in Scotland.[3] They had two sons and three dau
2 CONC ghters, including
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Scott, Earl of Dalkeith (1721–1750)
2 CONT Following her death, it was said by Lady Louisa Stuart that the duke "plunged into such low amours, and lived so entirely with the lowest company, that, although he resided constantly in the neighbourhood of London, his person was
2 CONC  scarcely known to his equals, and his character fell into utter contempt."[4] According to his will, he also had several illegitimate children by two other mothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Subsequently, the earl married Alice Powell and had further children. Both of his legitimate sons predeceased him, so he was succeeded by his grandson Henry Scott, 3rd Duke of Buccleuch.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-669263086/jane-scott-born-douglas-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 24 2019, 17:
2 CONC 24:28 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Douglas-3409
2 CONT * https://yourroots.com/tree/person/lady-douglas-1701-1729--wxiykrrwxceuj
2 CONT * https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/Jane_Douglas_(1701-1729)
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/76080385/jane-scott
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Jane Douglas was the daughter of James Douglas, 2nd Duke of Queensberry, and Mary Boyle.
2 CONT She married Francis Scott, 2nd Duke of Buccleuch, son of James Scott, Earl of Dalkeith, and Lady Henrietta Hyde, on 5 April 1720 at Earl of Rochester's House, Privy Gardens, Whitehall, London, England.
2 CONT She died aged 28 at Langley, Buckinghamshire, England.
2 CONT She was buried at St Mary's Church the private chapel at Dalkeith Castle, Scotland.
