1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir William Douglas, [Baronet [S 1625] of Ardit</strong>, otherwise Glenbervie, son and heir by 1st wife; born about 1690; was an Advocate of som eminence, and from 1726 to 1745 was annually chosen as Provost of the city 
2 CONC of St Andrews; was Inspector of the Customs on Tobacco in Scotland. He succeeded to the Baronetcy, February 1748. He married about 1718, Elizabeth, daughter of John Douglas, of Garvald, by Elizabeth, daughter of William and Isabel
2 CONC  Douglas. He died s.p. 23 July 1764, in his 75th year. His widow died 11 May 1777."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n303/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 284
2 CONT
2 CONT == Baronetcy of Nova Scotia ==
2 CONT <strong>Douglas</strong>
2 CONT * created 28 May and sealed 18 August 1625
2 CONT * Preceded by: [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Robert-Douglas-of-Ardit-4th-Baronet/6000000018521582589 Sir Robert Douglas of Ardit, 4th Baronet]
2 CONT * Succeeded by: [http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Robert-Douglas-of-Ardit-6th-Baronet/6000000018521668442 Sir Robert Douglas of Ardit, 6th Baronet]
