1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == HENRY CUNNINGHAM OF BOQUHAN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Scottish Whig politician; Commissioner justiciary for Highlands in 1701 and 1702; Muster Master General in Scotland, 1715-16; Commissioner for the forfeited estates, 1716-25; Provost of Inverkeithing, 1720; He sat i
2 CONC n the House of Commons from 1709 to 1734; He was given the post of Governor of Jamaica, but died two months after landing there. A description of Cunningham appears in the introduction to Scott's historical novel ‘’Rob Roy’’'''</b
2 CONC lockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henry Cunningham of Boquhan, here treated, was the only son of William Cunningham of Boquhan and his first wife Margaret Erskine, daughter of David Erskine, 2nd Lord Cardross. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Cunningham#cit
2 CONC e_note-HOP-1 Wikipedia]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henry Cunningham of Boquhan, here treated, died in Jamaica on 12 February 1736: "He fell by an act of his own intemperance at a public entertainment." [https://www.ucl.ac.uk/lbs/person/view/2146663557 Legacies of British Slaver
2 CONC y: Henry Cunningham]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henry Cunningham of Boquhan, here treated, married Jean Lennox daughter of John Lennox of Woodhead, Campsie, Stirling. They did not have any children. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Cunningham#cite_note-HOP-1 Wikipedia]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1738: Note of Infeftments affecting the Lands and Estate of deceased Henry Cunningham of Boquhan, Stirlingshire; and relative papers. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f1999&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=henry+cunningham&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1700&dt=1750&di=nNational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Morton, reference GD150/1999]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1738: Moses Buchanan of Glens v Helen Cunningham, sister of the deceased Henry Cunningham of Boquhan, Governor of Jamaica: Passive titles. Summons only in process. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details
2 CONC .aspx?reference=CS228%2fB%2f2%2f88&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=boquhan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1700&dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Court of Session: Unextracted processes, 1st arrangement, Adams-Dalrymple office, reference CS22
2 CONC 8/B/2/88]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
