1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY ELEANOR CAMPBELL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Eleanor Campbell, youngest daughter of James, second Earl of Loudoun, and his wife Margaret Montgomery. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/508/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 508]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Eleanor Campbell married, James, first Viscount Primrose, with whom she had four children. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/110/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 110]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Eleanor Campbell married Lord Stair in March 1707-8. After his death Lady Stair resided in Edinburgh and was an important person in Edinburgh Society. She died there on 21 November 1759, and was buried, on 24 November, at 
2 CONC Kirkliston. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/154/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 154]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children of First Marriage ==
2 CONT
