2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Howard, 10th Duke of Norfolk, Earl Marshal (1 December 1720 – 31 August 1786), the son of Henry Charles Howard (c. 1668–1720) and Mary Aylward (c. 1670–1747). He married Catherine Brockholes (before 1724–1784), daughter of
2 CONC  John Brockholes, on 8 November 1739. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of Duke of Norfolk in 1777 after the death of Edward Howard, 9th Duke of Norfolk
2 CONT
2 CONT  On the 9th Duke's death without a male heir, the title of "Duke of Norfolk" passed to his cousin Charles Howard (1720-1786), 10th Duke, the son of Henry Charles Howard, Lord of Greystoke (d.1720) and great grandson of Henry Frede
2 CONC rick Howard, Earl of Arundel & Surrey (1608-1652) who was also the great grandfather of the 9th Duke.. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Howard, 10th Duke of Norfolk died on 31 August 1786 at age 65. He was succeeded by his son, Charles Howard, 11th Duke of Norfolk.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_Howard,_10th_Duke_of_Norfolk
