1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Theodosia Bligh, 10th Baroness Clifton, was an English peer, born Theodosia Hyde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baroness Clifton was the third child and second daughter of Edward Hyde, 3rd Earl of Clarendon and Katherine Hyde, 8th Baroness Clifton. Her mother's title went first to her brother Edward Hyde, 9th Baron Clifton, but after his de
2 CONC ath from a 'surfeit of drinking', she succeeded as the 10th Baroness Clifton, of Leighton Bromswold on 12 February 1713.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baroness Clifton married John Bligh, MP for Athboy, soon afterwards, on 24 August 1713 at Westminster Abbey. They had six children and Baroness Clifton died in childbirth in 1722. She was buried on 15 August 1722 at Westminster Ab
2 CONC bey. Baroness Clifton's title passed to her second son, Edward. Her husband John was created Baron Clifton of Rathmore in 1721, and after her death was further elevated as Viscount Darnley and later Earl of Darnley in the Peerage 
2 CONC of Ireland (Theodosia's ancestors, the Dukes of Lennox, had also been Earls of Darnley in Scotland).
2 CONT
2 CONT The portrait called "Lady Theodosia Bligh, Countess of Glandore" painted in the manner of John Vanderbank the younger is now thought to be of her mother, Baroness Clifton. It is now in the collection of Castle Ward, County Down.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children; Lady Ann Bligh (died 7 February 1789) Lady Mary Bligh (died 4 March 1791) George Bligh (died 31 October 1714) Edward Bligh, 2nd Earl of Darnley (9 November 1715 – 22 July 1747) John Bligh, 3rd Earl of Darnley (28 Septemb
2 CONC er 1719 – 31 July 1781) Lady Theodosia Bligh (1722–20 May 1777), married William Crosbie, 1st Earl of Glandore.
