1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Campbell of Stackpole Court and Cawdor (1695–1777)''' - a British politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT s/o Sir Alexander Campbell, MP in the Scottish Parliament, & Elizabeth, d/o  Sir John Lort, 2nd Baronet, of Stackpole Court, Pembrokeshire
2 CONT
2 CONT x 1726, Mary, d/o Lewis Pryse, of Gogerddan, Cardiganshire
2 CONT
2 CONT *3 sons & 3 daughters, including possibly *Anne Campbell *John Campbell-Hooke *Pryse Campbell*Lt.-Col. Alexander Campbell
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Life
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was educated at Lincoln's Inn (1708) and Clare College, Cambridge (1711)
2 CONT * and succeeded his mother to the Stackpole estate in 1714 
2 CONT * and his grandfather Sir Hugh Campbell to estates in Nairnshire (Cawdor), Inverness-shire, and Argyll in 1716. Stackpole Court became the family home.
2 CONT * He was elected Member of Parliament (MP) for Pembrokeshire in 1727, sitting until 1747.
2 CONT *  He afterwards represented Nairnshire from 1747 to 1754, Inverness Burghs from 1754 to 1761 and Corfe Castle from 1762 to 1768.
2 CONT * He was also the Lord Commissioner of the Admiralty (1736–42) and Lord Commissioner of the Treasury (1746–54).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Campbell_of_Cawdor
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''John Campbell of Cawdor'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p4736.htm#i47360
2 CONT
2 CONT John Campbell of Cawdor was born in 1695.1 He married Mary Pryse, daughter of Lewis Pryse, on 30 April 1726.1 He died on 6 September 1777.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sir Alexander Campbell of Cawdor, younger and Elizabeth Lort.2 He held the office of Lord of the Treasury.1 He held the office of Lord of the Admiralty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Campbell of Cawdor and Mary Pryse
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Anne Campbell+2 d. 26 May 1812
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.John Hooke Campbell-Hooke+2
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Pryse Campbell+2 d. 14 Dec 1768
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.Lt.-Col. Alexander Campbell+2 d. Nov 1785
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 729. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pee
2 CONC rage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
