3 NOTE I have invested kensington where Mary was not it turns out it's another Mary whitfield a baby that is there and could not possible be the Mary whitfield that married Archibald Campbell 3rd so did not die in 1723 .
3 NOTE Hi Mary Ann Whitfield did not die in 1723 it turns out that Mary whitfield was adopted
4 CONT  (likely a soldiers promise to another in this case Archibalds father) 
4 CONT by Archbald Campbell 3rd family Mary was known as Mary Campbell  at that point part of the Campbell family this how Archibald Campbell 3rd and Mary Whitfield meet and latter married and there by Mary whitfield then had Campbell as
4 CONC  her married name as well Archibald Campbell 3rd and Mary had a daughter her name was Sophia Campbell born in 1773.
4 CONT
4 CONT Mary whitfield can be found in insurance documents in regent street London. insurance was by John Thomas barber Beaumonts company . John Thomas barber Beaumont was the husband of Sophia Campbell .
4 CONT John Thomas barber Beaumont was the son inlaw of Mary Whitfield. 
4 CONT
4 CONT There is also documents on Sophia baptisms record Recording Archibald Campbell and Mary. 
4 CONT
4 CONT And a court case where Archibald Campbell,s 3rd father died and his nieces tried to stop Mary whitfield AKA Mary Campbell from inheritance of property believed to be Regent street because Archibalds Father inheritance was from his
4 CONC  brother John and John's daughters where unhappy with Mary whitfield nee Campbell inheritance from Archibalds Father. 
4 CONT
4 CONT Archibalds Father died around 1743 not 1703 followed by one of his sons John which had 5 daughters and the family line of John died out .
