2 ADDR
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Table of Contents for Summary of the Memoirs of the Chiefs of Grants, pg. xiv:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=byANAAAAYAAJ&pg=PR14&lpg=PR14&dq=Marion+Dalrymple+Ludovick&source=bl&ots=bVn3l1KjE8&sig=ox7yNq_Wpt4mw8RUY19aFyaZZKo&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwij4KDX2YHQAhVll1QKHSm6BkQQ6AEIKTAE#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT XVII - Sir Ludovick Grant of Grant, Baronet, Marion Dalrymple (of North Berwick), his first wife, Lady Margaret Ogilvie (of Findlater), his second wife. 1747-1773.
2 CONT *Birth in 1707; becomes Laird of Luss, 1724; marriage with Marion, daughter of Sir Hew Dalrymple, (start pg. 393)
2 CONT *His father's displeasure at his marriage; Lovat's intercession; is admitted advocate,
2 CONT *Death of his first wife; his second marriage with Lady Margaret Ogilvie (of Findlater),
2 CONT *Mr. Grant resigns the estate of Luss; becomes Member of Parliament for the County of Moray,
2 CONT *The loyalty of the Clan Grant to King George the Second; landing of Prince Charles,
2 CONT *President Forbes in the North; Sir John Cope's march to Inverness; Mr. Grant's offer of assistance,
2 CONT *Mr. Grant urged to join Sir John; the Clan resolute to defend themselves; trouble in Urquhart,
2 CONT *Scheme of independent companies; Lord President Forbes and his conduct of affairs,
2 CONT *Mr. Grant summoned by William, Marquis of Tullibardine, to aid the cause of the Stewarts,
2 CONT *Protects Strathspey; tenants of Urquhart intercepted by Colonel Macdonald,
2 CONT *Assembles a body of men to relieve Urquhart; marches to Inverness; marauders leave Urquhart,
2 CONT *Lord Lewis Gordon's attempt to induce Mr. Grant to join the Jacobites,
2 CONT *Sends an independent company to Lord Loudoun; proposal to raise a second company,
2 CONT *President Forbe's policy in distributing the independent companies; loyalty of the Grants,
2 CONT *Lord Lewis Gordon and others pressing men to join the Prince; Mr. Grant marches to Keith,
2 CONT *Cooperates with the Lord of Macleod, who had cross the Spey; occupies Cullen House,
2 CONT *Remonstrance from Lord Lewis Gordon; advance to Strathbogie; rebels retire to Aberdeen,
2 CONT *Lord Loudoun intimates that he cannot take Mr. Grant's clan into pay,
2 CONT *Mr. Grant leaves a party to protect the district; returns to Castle Grant; disaffection in Urquhart,
2 CONT *His opinion that all available forces should be redeployed; defeat of Macleod at Invernuie,
2 CONT *Consternation at Elgin; Sir Archibald Grant's consultation with Lord Loudoun at Inverness,
2 CONT *Mr. Grant's effectual attempts to keep the people of Urquhart from joining the rebels,
2 CONT *Address to the King; defeat of the Royal army at Falkirk; Lord Loudoun writes for intelligence,
2 CONT *Mr. Grant assembles 600 men; requests arms; rout of May; Castle of Inverness taken,
2 CONT *Instructed to raise his clan for the King; marches towards Aberdeen 24th February 1746
2 CONT *Joins the Duke of Cumberland at Aberdeen; ordered to advance to Invernuie, 9th March,
2 CONT *The Duke of Cumberland disbands the militia; Mr. Grant resumes his parliamentary duties,
2 CONT *Death of his father; Sir Ludovick retires from Parliament, 1761, death, 1773; poem in his honour
2 CONT *Marriages, Lovat's account of wedding festivities,
2 CONT *His children, (pg. 440)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Ludovic Grant, Baronet [S 1645] of Grant</strong>, formerly (1719-32) Ludovic Colquhoun of Luss, 2nd but 1st surviving son and heir, born 13 January 1707; received from his father, in 1719, the Colquhoun estates, and 
2 CONC accordingly continued to bear the name of Colquhoun. These he endeavoured, unsuccessfully, to retain after the fee expectant of the Grant estates had, in 1735, been made over to him on the death of his elder brother, Humphrey Gran
2 CONC t, who died v.p. and unmarried 1732. He thereupon took the name Grant; was M.P. for Elgin and Forres-shire (three Parliaments), 1741-61, and succeeded to the Baronetcy, 16 January 1746/7. He married firstly, Marion, 2nd daughter o
2 CONC f the Hon. Hew Dalrymple, 1st Baronet [S 1638], by Marion, daughter of Sir Robert Hamilton. She, who was born 6 July 1636, died s.p.m. He married secondly, November 1735, Margaret, eldest of the two daughters of James (Oglivy), 5t
2 CONC h Earl of Findlater [S], and 2nd Earl of Seafield [S], by Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas (Hay), 6th Earl of Kinnoul [S]. She died 20 February 1757. He died 18 March 1773."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n313/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 295
