1 TITL Lt. Gen.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Lt.-Gen. Francis Grant''' was born on 10 August 1717.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Sir James Grant of Grant, 6th Bt. and Anne Colquhoun.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Catherine Sophia Cox, daughter of Joseph Cox and Katharine Sophia Herbert, on 17 March 1763.4 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 30 December 1781 at age 64.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Ensign in 1739 in the service of the 42nd Highlanders.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Captain in 1743.5 He gained the rank of Major in 1745.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Lieutenant-Colonel in 1755.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Seven Years War.5 He gained the rank of Colonel in 1758.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Brigadier in 1758.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) between 1768 and 1774.6 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Major-General in 1770.5 He fought in the Battle of Ticonderoga.4 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Lieutenant-General in 1777.5 He lived at Dumphail, Elgin, Scotland.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lt.-Gen. Francis Grant
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Lt.-Col. Robert Monckton Grant+5 b. bt 1758 - 1761
2 CONT
