1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "VII. <strong>Roderick Mackenzie, seventh of Redcastle</strong>, known among his countrymen as "Ruairi Ban." He married in 1730, Hannah Anna Murdoch of Cambodden, Galloway, with issue — 
2 CONT * Kenneth, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * Captain John, who by the will of the then proprietor, he having had no son of his own to leave it to, succeeded as VI. of Kincraig. 
2 CONT * Alexander and Roderick, died in infancy, 
2 CONT * Margaret, who on the 29th of November, 1755, married Sir Alexander Mackenzie, third Baronet and X. of Gairloch, with issue. She died on the 1st of September, 1759. 
2 CONT * Mary, who was born in 1732, and died, unmarried, at Lettoch, Redcasde, in 1828, aged 96 years. 
2 CONT * Elizabeth, who was born in 1746, and married in August 1782, Major-General Colin Mackenzie, with issue — Alexander Wedderburn, who died, unmarried, on the 4th of January, 1838, at Park House, Dingwall ; and Hannah Margaret Cochr
2 CONC ane, who died, unmarried, on the 2nd of February, 1858, at Golder's Green, Hendon. 
2 CONT * Christina, who was born in 1749. 
2 CONT * Jean, who was born in 1752, married Robert Anderson, Glasgow, and died, in 1819, without issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Roderick's wife died at Redcastle on the 21st of April, 1755, in the 39th year of her age. He died at Inverness on the 10th of May, 1785, and was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmackenz00mack#page/540/mode/2up History of the Mackenzies, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1894; page 541
