2 CONT "Roderick Mor had twelve other sons and two daughters, of whose history very little is known. One of the sons, either '''John or William''', married, with issue — at least two sons — the '''Rev. Hugh Mackenzie''', who was born in 
2 CONC 1771, and was for fourteen years Baptist minister at St. Ives, where he died and was buried in 1836. Hugh married, with issue — a son and daughter, both without issue. The second son,''' ALEXANDER MACKENZIE''', was born in 1772, a
2 CONC nd married in 1795, Helen, daughter of John Donaldson, Dunfermline, factor for the Earl of Dundonald, with issue — (1) William, who was born in 1797 and died in infancy ; (2) '''John DONALDSON MACKENZIE''', surgeon, who was born i
2 CONC n 1803, and practised his profession in Jersey. He married, in 1840, Emma Caroline, daughter of John Landseer, and sister of the eminent painter, Sir Edwin Landseer"
