1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 DEC 1750
1 OCCU Merchant in London
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from http://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/431/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT XIII. John Udny of Udny and the Newburgh. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He represented the county of Aberdeen in Parliament, 1703-1706; married, March, 1701, the Lady Martha Gordon, daughter of George, first Earl of Aberdeen, and Lord High Chancellor of Scotland, and had issue :— 
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Alexander, his successor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT II. George, merchant in London, d. s. p. 
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Anne, married Charles Eraser of Inverallochy, and died 24 August, 1753, leaving issue: William Fraser, afterwards of Udny ; 1. Martha Eraser, wife of Colin M'Kenzie of Kilcoy, county Ross ; 2. Eliza Eraser, who died unmarried
2 CONC . These ladies were served co-heiresses of their brother, William, in the lands of Muchalls and Inverallochy. Mrs. M'Kenzie is represented by Sir Colin M'Kenzie of Kilcoy, Bart., heir of line of Udny, and from her second son is de
2 CONC scended Colonel Eraser of Castle Eraser. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT from http://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/597/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Newburgh ... churchyard has been recently enclosed. Within it is the mausoleum of the Udny family, and there are several monuments within it to members of that family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Another is " In memory of Mrs. Mary Udny, widow of George Udny, Esq., died 16 December, 1807, aged 91. 'Esteemed and respected during life.'" 
2 CONT
2 CONT V. "George Udny, Esq., died 12 December, 17S0. 'Who never injured any man, and did all the good in his power.' " 
