1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Fraser, fifth Lord Saltoun of the Fraser line and fourteenth from the first creation</strong>. He was born on 10 October 1720. He entered the Army and obtained a commission in the Royal Marines. Succeeded his broth
2 CONC er in 1751 ; was interested in politics, and often voted at the elections of Representative Peers. He took no part in active affairs, and died on 30 August 1781 at the age of sixty-one. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his cousin Eleanor, daughter of John Gordon of Kinellar, who survived him, and died in 1800 ; by her he had seven children : 
2 CONT * Alexander, who succeeded as fifteenth Lord Saltoun. 
2 CONT * George, born 12 June 1759, and died in infancy the same year. 
2 CONT * John, born 18 January 1762, and died 6 June 1772. 
2 CONT * George, born 29 March 1763. He went into the Army, serving in the 42nd and 60th Regiments ; he held a captain's commission in the 59th, and died unmarried at Nevis in the "West Indies on 8 January 1799. 
2 CONT * Henrietta, born 20 July 1757, and died unmarried. in 1809. 
2 CONT * Mary, born 27 October 1760, and died unmarried in 1826. 
2 CONT * Eleanora, born 29 March 1766 ; married, first, 29 August 1786, to Sir George Ramsay of Bamff, who died in 1790 ; and secondly, 6 July 1792, to Lieut.-General Campbell of Lochnell, but had no issue by either husband."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/446/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VII, page 446
