2 CONT "James, Count Leslie,
2 CONT
2 CONT "Seventeenth Baron of Balquhain.
2 CONT
2 CONT "James, Count Leslie, born 25th May 1711, eldest son of George, Count Leslie, sixteenth Baron of Balquhain, by the Honourable Margaret Elphinsone his spouse, succeeded on the death of his father, 17th June 1715, as seventeenth Bar
2 CONC on of Balquhain, being then a child in his fourth year.
2 CONT
2 CONT "His mother, having been left the tutor of her children, resolved to bring them up Protestants, as is shown in the following evidence.  The Honourable Mary Elphinstone, wife of Thomas Buchan of Cairnbulg, advocate, stated that her
2 CONC  sister, the Honourable Margaret Elphinstone, married George Leslie of Balquhain in 1706; that George Leslie and his sisters were all bigoted papists; that she knew there was a popish chapel in their house, and a popish priest alw
2 CONC ays kept at Fetternear; that when her brother-in-law, Count George Leslie, died in 1715, his widow, her sister, sent for the popish priest, and desired him to pack up the popish trinkets, vestments, baubles, and many popish books,
2 CONC  and to carry them away, which he accordingly did; and that she was resolved to bring up her children, James and Ernest, and to educate them, as Protestants, which she did.  The Honourable Mrs. Buchan added that the family of Balq
2 CONC uhain had then several trinkets and vestments which, she was informed, had been sent from Germany by James, Count Leslie, for the use of the chapel and priest.  These church vestments and plate, which were thus sent away were of t
2 CONC he richest brocaded stuffs, gold and silver cloth, and precious metals and jewels, being made out of articles taken from the Turks in various battles in which Field-Marshal James, Count Leslie, had defeated them.  Besides these, m
2 CONC any other valuable articles were carried away from Fetternear, amongst the rest many family portraits, much silver plate and rich furniture.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Not content with this, the Honourable Margaret Elphinstone also induced her son, Ernest, Count Leslie, eighteenth Baron of Balquhain, to dismember the family estates.  She had a locality, that is the revenue of certain lands for 
2 CONC her jointure on the lands of Insch and Boddam, belonging to the Balquhain estates.  After her husband’s death, about 1720, she married Sir James Gordon of Park, by whom she had a son, James Gordon, styled of Cobairdy, and she prev
2 CONC ailed on her son Ernest, when he succeeded to the Balquhain estates, to dispone part of the lands of Insch, and the lands of Boddam, to the said James Gordon, his uterine brother, which was in defraud of the deed of entail made by
2 CONC  Count Patrick Leslie, fifteenth Baron, in 1700.  Count Authony Leslie, nineteenth Baron of Balquain, sought to reduce this iniquitous dispostion, but he did not succeed, as will be shown hereafter.
2 CONT
2 CONT "While still a minor, Count James Leslie went abroad to travel, and on his way home again he died at Paris, 29th January 1731, in the twentieth year of his age, unmarried.  Some time afterwards his body was brought over to Scotlan
2 CONC d, and interred in the old chapel at Fetternear.  In digging the grave for Violet Dalzel, widow of John Leslie, twenty-second Baron of Balquhain, in September 1836, his leaden coffin was dug up, and was again replaced above the co
2 CONC ffin of Mrs. Leslie in the same grave.  There was found lying on the lid of the coffin a long piece of metal rounded at one end and pointed at the other, on which were engraved the family crest, a griffin’s head, and the motto, “G
2 CONC rip fast”, with the following inscription:--
2 CONT
2 CONT “ ‘Jacobus Leslie de Balquhain
2 CONT
2 CONT   ‘Natus 24 Maij. 1711.
2 CONT
2 CONT   ‘Obiit Parisiis. 29 Januarii 1731.’
2 CONT
2 CONT “The following inscription is engraved on a metal plate preserved at Fetternear House:--
2 CONT
2 CONT “                           S.D.G.
2 CONT
2 CONT “   In memoriam Iuvenis ingentis speciei,
2 CONT
2 CONT “                          Dum vixit
2 CONT
2 CONT “          Majoris spei si fata sivissent
2 CONT
2 CONT “     Honorandi Domini D. Jacobi Leslie
2 CONT
2 CONT “                       de Balquhain.
2 CONT
2 CONT “           Cujus si prosapiam spectes
2 CONT
2 CONT “                      Quid antiquius ?
2 CONT
2 CONT “            In Martis et Minervae scholis
2 CONT
2 CONT “                    Quid illustrious ?
2 CONT
2 CONT “      Si Rem familiarem, amplam satis
2 CONT
2 CONT “                    Honesti partam.
2 CONT
2 CONT “       Industria et bonis artibus auctam
2 CONT
2 CONT “                  Et adhuc augendam.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                            Repearies.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                 Si corporis dignitatem
2 CONT
2 CONT “               Statura erecta et procera.
2 CONT
2 CONT “           Vultu erecto. Gravi, verecundo.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                       Hilari tamen.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                         Et amabili.
2 CONT
2 CONT “        Pietatem, si spectes, Dei, Principis
2 CONT
2 CONT “                           Et Patriae
2 CONT
2 CONT “                    Cultorem Invenies.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                   Sanctissimum simul
2 CONT
2 CONT “                         Ac fidissimum
2 CONT
2 CONT “     Si probitatem, sobrius erat et equanimus
2 CONT
2 CONT “             Omnibus aequus, omnibus gratis.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                       Facile omnes ferebat
2 CONT
2 CONT “                             Et patiebatur.
2 CONT
2 CONT “               Nunquam se praeponens alijs.
2 CONT
2 CONT “             Ita laudem inveniebat et amicos,
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                 Parabat.
2 CONT
2 CONT “      Verbis inerat fides, Comitas, et humanitas.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                   Factis aequitas et charitas.
2 CONT
2 CONT “     Parenti optimae, praeceptoribus paedagogis
2 CONT
2 CONT “                              Et Tutoribus
2 CONT
2 CONT “                        Semper morigerus.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                    Nec prodigus nec parcus,
2 CONT
2 CONT “                 Qui dum in exteras Regiones
2 CONT
2 CONT “                      Ad Ingenium Exceolendum
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                 Et Majorem
2 CONT
2 CONT “Cognitionis & experientiae suppellectilem struendam
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                  Tendebat.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                Pariiis, A.D. MDCCXXXI. Jarij 29
2 CONT
2 CONT “                               Fatis concessit
2 CONT
2 CONT “                           Et quod mortale fuit
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                    Hic posuit.
2 CONT
2 CONT “       Hunc tantum terries ostendunt fata nex ultra
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                   Esse sinunt.
2 CONT
2 CONT “                     Qualem amisit patria civem
2 CONT
2 CONT “                    Uno avulso, non deficit alter
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                       Aureus.
2 CONT
2 CONT “The following invitation addressed to John Leslie seventh Laird of Warthill, by Count Ernest Leslie, sighteenth Baron of Balquhain, to attend the funeral of his brother, Count James Leslie, seventeenth baron, is preserved amont t
2 CONC he family papers at Fetternear:--
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir, -- The Corpse of James Lesley of Balquhain, my brother, lyeing in Saint Paules Chappell of Aberdeen are to be transported from thence, and Interred in his Chappell at Fetterneir, upon the twenty-third day of Aprile current. 
2 CONC  Your presence here at eight of the clock before noon To witness the same, Is earnestly Intreated by Sir, your most humble servant,
2 CONT
2 CONT “                                                              Ernest Leslie.
2 CONT
2 CONT “   Aberdeen, Pitfodles Lodgeing,
2 CONT
2 CONT “            16th Aprile 1731.
2 CONT
2 CONT “Count James Leslie, seventeenth Baron of Balquain, dying unmarried 29th January 1731, was succeeded by his brother, Count Ernest Leslie, eighteenth baron.”
