1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From http://ro.com/~rts2/ancestry/d52.html#P97 :
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander FAIRLEY , Sr. was born in 1753 in Argyllshire, Scotland. He died on 25 DEC 1827 in Richmond Co. NC. He was buried in Richmond Co. NC (Alexander Fairly Cemetery).
2 CONT
2 CONT This family name has been spelled Fairley, Fairly, Farley, etc. His will in Richmond Co. NC, probated JAN, 1828, was signed Alexander Fairley, which should prove the correct spelling of the name.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 1785 tax list for Richmond County, NC, called a State Census, "Alex_r Farley" was enumerated as age 21 or over but less than 60 years and had no other persons in his household. John Farley and Arch_d Farley were enumerated 
2 CONC separately with several children in each household. The tax list thus indicates that Alexander Fairley was born in 1764 or earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1790 Census - Richmond Co. NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexr Fairley, 2 slaves
2 CONT
2 CONT Free white males 16 & older (b. bef. 1774) - 1 <Alex>
2 CONT
2 CONT Free white males under 16 (b. 1774-1790) - 0
2 CONT
2 CONT Free white females - 0
2 CONT
2 CONT Living next door to John Fairley (probably father and/or brother John)
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Our Native Heath":
2 CONT
2 CONT Sheriff's Tax Book for Richmond Co., 1792-1793, show an Alexander Fairly.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810 Census - Richmond Co. NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Fairley, p. 202, 14 slaves
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 males b. 1800-1810
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 males b. 1784-1794
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 male b. bef. 1765
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 females b. 1800-1810
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 females b. 1794-1800
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 female b. 1765-1784
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond Co. NC, 1812 tax list, Acres White Polls
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Fairley 2795 8
2 CONT
2 CONT 1820 Census - Richmond Co. NC
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Fairley, p. 218
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 males b. 1804-1810
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 male b. 1775-1794
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 male b. bef. 1775
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 females b. 1794-1804
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 female b. bef. 1775
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 persons engaged in agriculture, 33 slaves
2 CONT
2 CONT <p.218 neighbors Caty McCarter, John McDonald, George Graham, Daniel McCall>
2 CONT
2 CONT The Last Will and Testament of Alexander Fairley was dated 13 DEC 1827 and was probated in the January Court, 1828. Recorded in Richmond County, NC, Will Book 1, Page 281.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: "Effy"
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons: Peter, Archibald (co-executor), John, Daniel
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters: Margaret ("Daniel McNair's wife"), Mary, Catherine
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandson: Alexander (son of Peter)
2 CONT
2 CONT Granddaughter: Margaret McEachin
2 CONT
2 CONT Son-in-law: Daniel McNair (co-executor)
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: Duncan McIntyre
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhoderick McRae
2 CONT
2 CONT Colin McArthur
2 CONT
