2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Houston, Baronet [S. 1668], of Houston, only s. and h; suc. to the Baronetcy, 11 Feb. 1722, and sold the much encumbered estate of Houston in 1740. He (though impotent) m. 12 Feb. 1744, at Edinburgh, his cousin Eleanor
2 CONC a, 1st da. of Charles (Cathcart), 8th Lord Cathcart [S.], by his 1st wife, Marion, only child of Sir John Shaw, 3d and last Baronet [S. 1687], of Greenock. She, who was b. in Edinburgh, 3 March 1720, brought him £3,500, but (thoug
2 CONC h aware before her marriage of her husband's state) sued for a divorce.(c) He d. s.p. in London 27 and was bur. 31 July 1751, at St. Martin's in the Fields.( a ) His widow d. 3 Nov. 1769, in her 50th year." [http://archive.org/str
2 CONC eam/cu31924092524408#page/n287/mode/2up Complete baronetage IV: 268-69]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4bz/houston01.php Stirnet: Houston 01]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Houston, Baronet [S. 1668], of Houston</strong>, s. and h. ; was M.P. for Linlithgowshire (three Paris.), 1708-15 ; Commissary of Glasgow ; suc. to the Baronetcy in Dec. 1717. He m. Margaret, da. of Sir John Shaw
2 CONC , 2d Baronet [S. 1687], of Greenock, by Margaret, da. of Sir Thomas Nicolson, 2d Baronet [S. 1637] of Carnock. He d. 11 Feb. 1722, " in the flower of his age," leaving his estate burdened with some 200,000 debt. His widow d. (a ye
2 CONC ar before her son) 29 Jan. 1750."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n287/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 268
