1 NOTE {geni:about_me} notę by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jakub Poniatowski of the Ciołek coat of arms was born on 24 January 1723 in Warsaw, in Warsaw Land, Masovian Voivodeship, Crown of the Kingdom of Poland, Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth. According to the parish record, he was born 
2 CONC at about four o’clock in the morning.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the same day, 24 January 1723, Jakub was baptized with water (chrzest z wody) at the Church of the Holy Cross in Warsaw. The parish record names him as the son of Stanisław Ciołek Poniatowski and Konstancja née Czartoryska.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism with water was an initial baptism performed without the full solemn ceremony. This form of baptism was used when the baptism of a child could not or should not be delayed. The available record confirms that Jakub was bapti
2 CONC zed with water on 24 January 1723. At present, there is no known information confirming that the full baptismal ceremony was completed later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Baptismal record of Jakub Poniatowski, Roman Catholic Parish of the Holy Cross in Warsaw, Baptism Register 1701-1729
