1 NOTE {geni:about_me} note by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Michał Ludwik Poniatowski of the Ciołek coat of arms was a son of Stanisław Poniatowski of the Ciołek coat of arms and Konstancja née Czartoryska.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the older brother of Michał Jerzy Poniatowski, the future Primate of Poland, and had the same first name, Michał.
2 CONT For a long time, Michał Ludwik was unknown to researchers of the Poniatowski family genealogy. Polish historian Krzysztof R. Prokop found information about him in old church records and published it in his work “Varia genealogiczn
2 CONC e XVII - XVIII wieku ze staropolskich metryk kościelnych z Warszawy i Wołczyna”. In a later publication, Prokop clearly describes Michał Ludwik as the older brother and namesake of the future Primate Michał Jerzy Poniatowski, prev
2 CONC iously unknown in genealogical studies of the Poniatowski family.
2 CONT
2 CONT The exact date of Michał Ludwik’s birth is not given in the published text. Prokop believes that he was most probably born in 1727. This conclusion is based on the fact that the ceremony held in Wołczyn on 5 September 1728 was not
2 CONC  his original baptism, but the solemn completion of the baptismal rites, in Polish “uroczyste dopełnienie chrztu”. The ceremony was performed by Stefan Rupniewski, Bishop of Łuck. Therefore, 5 September 1728 is a confirmed date of
2 CONC  this church ceremony, but it should not be used as the date of Michał Ludwik’s birth or original baptism.
2 CONT The later life of Michał Ludwik is unknown. The source discussed here does not give an exact record of his death. Prokop concludes that the boy must have died in early childhood, in any case before 1736. This conclusion is based o
2 CONC n the fact that on 12 October 1736 Stanisław Poniatowski and Konstancja Czartoryska had another son, who was given the name Michał Jerzy. Prokop connects the repeated use of the name Michał with the fact that the older Michał Ludw
2 CONC ik had already died by that time.
2 CONT
2 CONT His younger brother, Michał Jerzy Poniatowski, was born on 12 October 1736 in Gdańsk and later became Bishop of Płock, Archbishop of Gniezno and Primate of Poland. The surviving baptismal record names his parents as Stanisław Cioł
2 CONC ek Poniatowski, Voivode of Masovia, and Konstancja of the Czartoryski family. The separate baptismal record for Michał Jerzy and the separate information about Michał Ludwik show that they were two different sons of Stanisław Poni
2 CONC atowski and Konstancja Czartoryska, not different names of the same person.
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on: Krzysztof R. Prokop, “Varia genealogiczne XVII - XVIII wieku ze staropolskich metryk kościelnych z Warszawy i Wołczyna”, Biuletyn Biblioteki Jagiellońskiej, 2004, information about Michał Ludwik on pp. 155-156, 166-167.
2 CONT Krzysztof R. Prokop, “Wypisy źródłowe do biografii polskich biskupów i opatów z czasów Rzeczypospolitej Obojga Narodów oraz niewoli narodowej doby zaborów (XVI - XIX w.). Część IX”, Archiwa, Biblioteki i Muzea Kościelne, 95, 2011.
