1 NOTE {geni:about_me} note by Natalia Gurko:
2 CONT
2 CONT =Teodor Feliks Poniatowski of the Ciołek coat of arms was a son of Stanisław Poniatowski of the Ciołek coat of arms and Konstancja née Czartoryska.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the children of this family who died young and for a long time were not included in the traditional genealogies of the Poniatowski family.
2 CONT On 3 July 1733, Teodor Feliks was baptized at St. John’s Church in Warsaw. His godparents were Teodor Czartoryski, provost of the Płock Cathedral Chapter, after whom the boy was named Teodor, and Antonina Rudzińska, daughter of Ka
2 CONC zimierz Rudziński, cup-bearer of Czersk.
2 CONT
2 CONT The parish registers of the Holy Cross Church in Warsaw also contain a record of the death of Teodor Poniatowski on 8 July 1740. The researcher Iwona M. Dacka-Górzyńska found and published this record in her study about previously
2 CONC  unknown children of Polish magnate families. In the record, Teodor is described as an eight-year-old son of the Poniatowski family.
2 CONT The information about Teodor is important for the history of the family because it shows that Stanisław Poniatowski and Konstancja Czartoryska had more children than were listed in older genealogies. Traditionally, eight children 
2 CONC were attributed to the couple, but research in parish registers has confirmed the existence of other children who died at a young age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Iwona M. Dacka-Górzyńska, “O nieznanych dzieciach magnaterii polskiej w świetle parafialnych metryk zmarłych kościoła św. Krzyża w Warszawie z lat 1670-1801. Wybrane przykłady”, Przegląd Historyczny, 2011, vol. 102, no. 3
2 CONC ; parish registers of St. John’s and Holy Cross parishes in Warsaw.
