1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph DOUGLAS Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name - I have seen it reported by many researchers that Joseph Jr., son of Joseph Douglas Sr. (1676-1756) of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Co., MD, had a middle name of "Hamilton".  However, I have seen no documentation of this middle name for Joseph Douglas Jr.  A Joseph Hamilton Douglas married a Rachel Bayard in Baltimore Co., MD in 1768.  But I have seen 
2 CONC no proof that this Joseph Hamilton Douglas was a son of Joseph Douglas Sr. of Charles Co., MD.  Joseph Douglas of Caroline Co., MD was appointed Captain on 14 May 1776.           
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth - date from the website of Frank Collins of Fort Mill, SC, www.collinsfactor.com.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1754/1757 - identified as "son Joseph Douglas" in the will of his father, Joseph Douglas; written 7 Jul 1754.  Joseph inherited "Smiths Fortune", 25 acres in Charles Co., MD; & 2 "young negros, James & Hannah", from his father; wi
2 CONC ll probated 21 Jun 1757.  [Note: Since Joseph was a minor, he probably did not take possession until he was 21 - @1768.]  Charles County Wills, Liber 30, folio 274.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1761 - identified as "brother Joseph Douglas" in the will of his half-brother, John Douglas; written 6 Jul 1761.  Joseph was to inherit 1/7 of John's estate; will probated 9 Dec 1761.  Charles County Wills, Liber 31, folio 487.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1766/ 1768 - identified as "son Joseph Douglas" in the will of his mother, Catherine Douglas; written 19 May 1766.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was named executor & was to inherit "negroes Quam & Winnes", silver spoons, & remainder of estate; will probated 9 May 1768.  Charles Co., MD Wills.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1768 - Joseph, along with his half brother Thomas Harris, executed the will of their mother, Catherine Douglas; 7 Jun 1768.  Charles County Wills.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1768 - A Joseph Hamilton Douglass married a Rachel Bayard in St. Paul's Parish, Baltimore Co. on 4 Apr 1768.  "St. Paul's Parish Records, 1700-1800", pg 53.  And the couple had 1 child, George Crispin, 2 Jan 1769.  "Maryland Marri
2 CONC ages, 1634-1777", Barnes;  & "St. Paul's Parish Records".  I have not seen documentation or proof that this Joseph Hamilton Douglas was a son of Joseph Douglas & Catherine Musgrave.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage - Joseph Douglas to Rebecca Nichols.  "The Douglas Family of Charles County, MD", article by Dr. Neil D. Thompson in "The American Genealogist", Vol 49, No 4, Oct 1973, pg 193-202.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1773 - Caroline County, MD created in 1773 from Dorchester & Queen Anne Counties, MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1775-1778 Census - William & Mary Parish, Upper Hundred, Charles Co., MD - Joseph Douglas.  "Maryland Records - Colonial, Revolutionary, County & Church from Original Sources" by Gais Marcus Brumbaugh, 1915, Vol I, pg 301.
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service - Revolutionary War; appointed Captain 14 May 1776; 14th Battalion of Caroline Co., MD.  Maryland Archives, Vol 11, pg 424.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1777 - owned "St. George's Regulation", 319 acres in Caroline Co., MD; 6 Aug 1777.  Caroline County Land Records, Liber A, folio 254.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1781-1783 - Justice of the Peace for Caroline Co., MD.  Maryland Archives, Vol 48, pg 45, 223, 341.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1783 - Charles Co., MD Tax Assessment - Joseph Douglas, 188 acres.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1783 - Lower Choptank District Hundred, Caroline Co., MD Tax Assessment  - Joseph Douglass, St. Georges 
2 CONT
2 CONT Regulation, 369 acres.  Maryland Archives, MSA S 1437.  [Note: Did Joseph own land in both counties?  Or was the land owned by different  2 Joseph Douglass?  The 1790 Census has a Joseph in both Caroline & Charles County.] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1786 - owned 100 acres in Caroline Co, MD; 30 Dec 1786.  Caroline County Land Records, Liber B, folio 202.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1790 Census  -  Caroline Co., MD - Joseph Douglass:  1 male over 16 (Joseph, 43); 3 males under 16 (Thomas, 15; Joseph, 6; John); 4 females (wife Rebecca, 40; Elizabeth, 12; Mary, 10; ? ).  [Note: There is also a  Joseph Douglass 
2 CONC in Charles Co., MD:  1 male over 16, 1 male under 16 & 6 females.  It is quite possible that this Joseph Douglass of Charles Co. is the Joseph who was assessed for 188 acres in 1783; & the Joseph Douglas counted in the 1775-1778 C
