2 CONC rhSource=7853 AncestryImage] James Smith Gender:	Male Spouse:	Mrs. Elizabeth Campbell Marriage Date:	13 Mar 1760 City:	Boston County:	Suffolk Source:	Family History Library, Salt Lake City, UT, Film # 0818093-0818095.
2 CONT * https://www.masshist.org/collection-guides/view/fa0343. She married first Thomas Campbell in 1755, and in 1760 she married 72-year-old John Smith, a sugar refiner who owned an estate at Brush Hill in Milton, Mass., property that
2 CONC  stayed in the Murray-Robbins family for generations. She became a widow for the second time in 1769, marrying Ralph Inman in 1771. She died without children in Milton, Mass. in 1785.
2 CONT * [https://www.bostonbasinhills.org/pages/milton-hills.html “ More about Milton's USGS-listed hills”] “ While the families living on these three Milton hills in the 1700s would have descendants that became magnates of commerce and
2 CONC  industry, judges, governors, senators, vice presidents, even a president, it’s James Smith’s second wife, Elizabeth (Murray) Campbell, Smith, Inman (1726-1785),6 who has one of the more interesting stories as she overcame social 
2 CONC barriers and persevered during the tumultuous times before and after the revolutionary war. ...”
