1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Lilias</strong>, 1st of three daughters and coheirs became, eventually, the heir to the considerable estates of her great uncle, the 6th Baronet. She was served his heir, of taillie, 28 August 1735. She married 11 June 17
2 CONC 35, her cousin, Alexander Montgomery of Coylsfield, co. Ayr, great grandson of Alexander, 6th Earl of Eglinton [S]. She obtained an Act of Paliament in 1759 to enable her to sell her estates, co. Renfrew, and purchase lands near h
2 CONC er husbands estates, co. Ayr. She died 18 November, her husand dying 28 December 1783. Their son and heir, Hugh on 30 October 1796, became Earl of Eglinton [S]."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n355/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 336
2 CONT --------------------
