1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * September 1704, d. 12 February 1781 
2 CONT * John Hope, 2nd Earl of Hopetoun was born on 7 September 1704.  
2 CONT * He was the son of Charles Hope, 1st Earl of Hopetoun and Lady Henrietta Johnstone.  
2 CONT * He married, firstly, Anne Ogilvy, daughter of James Ogilvy, 5th Earl of Findlater and Lady Elizabeth Hay, on 14 September 1733.  
2 CONT * He married, secondly, Jane Oliphant, daughter of Robert Oliphant, on 30 October 1762.  
2 CONT * He married, thirdly, Lady Elizabeth Leslie, daughter of Alexander Leslie, 7th Earl of Leven and Elizabeth Monypenny, on 10 June 1767.  
2 CONT *      
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hope, 2nd Earl of Hopetoun succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Hope on 26 February 1742. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 2nd Viscount of Aithrie on 26 February 1742.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Hopetoun on 26 February 1742. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of a Lord of Police [Scotland] between 1744 and 1760. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1747 he was appointed Curator Bonis (Trustee in Lunacy) for his half-uncle, 4th Earl of Annandale and Hartfell. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Lord High Commissioner to the General Assembly of the Church of Scotland in 1754.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 12 February 1781  at age 76.
