1 NOTE [Knox.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT [v07t0516.ged]
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael Johnstone Kenan served with the North Carolina militia during the American REvolutionary War.  He held the rank of captain in the Duplin Militia and also served in the state militia, Wilmington District, following the war'
2 CONC s end.
2 CONT He was a member of the Continental Congress in 1777 representing North Carolina.  He was one of the signers of Duplin County's Oath of Allegiance to the United States in 1777.
2 CONT Sometime between October 1793 and September 1794, the Kenans moved from North Carolina to Jaspar County, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Alvaretta Kenan, Daughters of the American Revolution
