1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hon. '''Jane Cathcart''' was born on 20 May 1754 at London, England. She died on 5 December 1790 at age 36 at Hanover Square, Mayfair, London, England.1 She was buried on 30 December 1790 at Dunkeld Cathedral, Dunk
2 CONC eld, Perthshire, Scotland.[1] As a result of her marriage, Hon. Jane Cathcart was styled as Duchess of Atholl on 26 December 1774. From 26 December 1774, her married name became Murray.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  daughter of Lt.-Gen. Sir Charles Schaw Cathcart, 9th Lord Cathcart and Jane Hamilton.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #  on 26 December 1774 at Grosvenor Place, St. George Hanover Square, London, England to Sir John Murray, 4th Duke of Atholl, son of Sir John Murray, 3rd Duke of Atholl and Lady Charlotte Murray, Baroness Strange, 1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hon. Jane Cathcart and Sir John Murray, 4th Duke of Atholl
2 CONT # Lady Amelia Sophia Murray+2 d. 19 Jun 1849
2 CONT # Lady Elizabeth Murray
2 CONT # John Murray, 5th Duke of Atholl1 b. 26 Jun 1778, d. 14 Sep 1846
2 CONT # Lt.-Gen. Sir James Murray, 1st Baron Glenlyon+1 b. 29 May 1782, d. 12 Oct 1837
2 CONT
