1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY ELIZABETH GLEN Countess of Dalhousie ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Elizabeth Glen, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Glen-of-Longcroft/6000000028124644426?through=6000000008006328166 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun
2 CONC 03pauluoft/page/103/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 103] and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Lucy-Downes/6000000217853039828?through=6000000008006328166. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?re
2 CONC ference=GD45%2f14%2f478&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+glen&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD45/14/478]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1757-77: Letters, mostly to Miss Elizabeth Glen, latterly Countess of Dalhousie, and to her husband concerning the estate in India of Mrs. Lucy Downes, Miss Glen's mother. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f14%2f478&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+glen&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/14/478]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 July 1768: Extract discharge by Agnes Glen, relict of David Bruce of Kinnaird, to George, Earl of Dalhousie, and Elizabeth Glen, now Countess of Dalhousie, niece of said Agnes, of a claim for maintenance of said Elizabeth as
2 CONC signed by the said David on 7 March 1758. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2633&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+glen&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scot
2 CONC land, Papers of the Ramsay Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/2633]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[ 1768 ]: Draft discharge by Agnes Glen, relict of David Bruce of Kinnaird, to George, Earl of Dalhousie, of sums due for aliment etc. to said David by Miss Betty Glen, his niece, now Countess of Dalhousie, assigned by said Dav
2 CONC id to said Agnes. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2634&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+glen&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay F
2 CONC amily, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/2634]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 September 1777: Instrument of cognition and sasine in favour of Elizabeth, Countess of Dalhousie, as heir to James Glen of Longcroft, formerly Governor of South Carolina, brother of Andrew Glen, her father, in tenements in Li
2 CONC nlithgow. Registered B.R.S. Linlithgow, 4 September 1777. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2648&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=andrew+glen&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Re
2 CONC cords of Scotland, Papers of the Ramsay Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/2648]'''
