2 CONT
2 CONT createdv.p. 5 Mar 1783 Baron Rawdon, of Rawdon in the County of York (Peerage of Great Britain)
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Feb 1817 Viscount Loudoun, Earl of Rawdon and Marquess of Hastings
2 CONT
2 CONT The Earldom of Moira was held by the Marquesses of Hastings from 13 Feb 1817 until 10 Nov 1868, when on the death without issue of Henry Weysford Charles Plantagenet [Rawdon-Hastings], 4th Marquess of Hastings, 5th Earl of Moira, 
2 CONC etc., the Marquessate of Hastings, the Earldoms of Moira and Rawdon, the Viscountcy of Loudoun and the two Baronies of Rawdon all became extinct
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Rawdon,_1st_Earl_of_Moira
2 CONT
2 CONT John Rawdon, 1st Earl of Moira (17 March 1720 – 20 June 1793), known as Sir John Rawdon, Bt, between 1724 and 1750 and as The Lord Rawdon between 1750 and 1762, was an Irish peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Background
2 CONT
2 CONT Rawdon was the only son of Sir John Rawdon, 3rd Baronet and Dorothy, daughter of Sir Richard Levinge, 1st Baronet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT
2 CONT Rawdon succeeded his father in the baronetcy in February 1724, aged three. In 1750 he was elevated to the Peerage of Ireland as Baron Rawdon, of Moira in the County of Down. In 1762 he was further honoured when he was made Earl of
2 CONC  Moira in the Irish peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Moira married, firstly, Helena Perceval, daughter of John Perceval, 1st Earl of Egmont and Lady Catherine Parker, on 10 November 1741. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Helena Rawdon, married Stephen Moore, 1st Earl Mountcashell and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Catherine Rawdon, married Joseph Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her death in June 1746 he married, secondly, Anne Hill, daughter of Trevor Hill, 1st Viscount Hillsborough and Mary Rowe, on 23 December 1746. They had no children. After her death in August 1751 he married, thirdly, Elizabe
2 CONC th Hastings, 16th Baroness Botreaux, daughter of Theophilus Hastings, 9th Earl of Huntingdon and Lady Selina Shirley, on 26 February 1752. They had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Selina Frances Rawdon (d. 1827), married George Forbes, 6th Earl of Granard and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Charlotte Adelaide Constantia Rawdon (d. 1834), married Hamilton Fitzgerald.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Anne Elizabeth Rawdon (1753–1813), married Thomas Brudenell-Bruce, 1st Earl of Ailesbury and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Theophilus Rawdon (John Trotter,1776)Francis Rawdon-Hastings, 1st Marquess of Hastings (1754–1826)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. John Theophilus Rawdon (1756–1808)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Moira died in June 1793, aged 73, and was succeeded by his eldest son by his third marriage, Francis, who had already been created Baron Rawdon in his own right in 1783 and was created Marquess of Hastings in 1816. The Counte
2 CONC ss of Moira died in April 1808.
