1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John George, fifth Lord Banff</strong> was born 18 February 1717, and succeeded his father 1718. Married, at the Fleet, London, 18 August 1735, Mary, daughter of Captain James Ogilvie. He was drowned, 29 July 1738, when b
2 CONC athing with Lord Deskford, afterwards sixth Earl of Findlater, at the Black Rocks near Oullen, and was buried at Banff, 1 August 1738. His widow married, secondly, the Rev. Thomas Kemp, D.D., Rector of St. Michael's, Crooked Lane,
2 CONC  London. Lord Banff dying without issue was succeeded by his brother."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/20/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. II, page 21
