1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>William Moir</strong>, born 1726, son of 1749 George M., min. of Kintore ; educated at Marischal College, Aberdeen, 1740-4; licen. by Presb. of Ellon 4th Oct. 1748 ; pres. by tutors of the Hon. William Gordon of Fyvie in N
2 CONC ov. 1748; ord. 27th April 1749; died 19th March 1794. He marr. 22nd Oct. 1776, Helen Constable,  who died at Aberdeen 26th Feb. 1817, aged 67, and had issue — 
2 CONT * George, M.A., Kingston, Jamaica, born 18th Dec. 1777, died 11th Sept. 1807 ; 
2 CONT * Katherine Jean, born 6th April 1779 (marr. 30th March 1800, John Dingwall of Rainieston, provost of Aberdeen).
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc06scot#page/256/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VI, page 257
1 FAMC @F6000000026828025788@
1 FAMS @F6000000022853763555@
1 RFN geni:6000000022854665058
1 SUBM @S6000000016612786622@
1 CHAN
2 DATE 04 MAY 2022
3 TIME 12:04:03
0 @I6000000022854826397@ INDI
1 NAME Agnes /Moir/
2 GIVN Agnes
2 SURN Moir
2 _MARNM Moir
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 1723 AND 1729
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1809
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Agnes</strong>, born 1723-9, married Alexander Rose, eldest son of Rose, Laird of Lethinty, Aberdeenshire, and died in 1809 at the manse of Auchterless. Her daughter, Jane Rose, b. 1754, married 1790 the Rev Alexander Rose
2 CONC , minister of Auchterless, also in the county of Aberdeen, and died in the town of that name 22d Sept. 1820, leaving two daughters — 
2 CONT * Agnes Rose, b. 1795, died unm. in 1827; and 
2 CONT * Jane Margaret Rose, b. 1796, m. 1823 the Rev John Johnston of Forgandenny, in the county of Perth, and died 26th Sept. 1832, leaving two sons and two daughters, viz., 
2 CONT ** John Robert Johnston, b. 1828, settled in New Zealand, married 1850, and died 1862, leaving two sons and four daughters ; 
2 CONT ** Alexander Rose Johnston, b. 1832, married 1866 Pauline, A. M., daughter of Alexander Farquhar of Glenesk, Aberdeenshire. Issue, two sons and four daughters
2 CONT ** Jane Taylor Johnston (eldest dau. of Rev J. Johnston), b. 1825, m. 1881 Andrew Paterson Reid of Tigh- na-mara, Roseneath, co. Dumbarton ; 
2 CONT ** Agnes Rose Johnston (2d dau.), b. 1830, married, 1869, Donald M. Macandrew, merchant, of Leith, and now of Torquay.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Gill of Savock, Andrew John Mitchell. [http://archive.org/stream/familiesofmoirby00gill#page/12/mode/2up The families of Moir and Byres]. Edinburgh : Scott & Ferguson, 1885. page 13
