1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Anstruther, Baronet [S. 1700], of Anstruther and Elie House</strong>, 1st but only surv. s. and h., b. 27 Dec. 1718, at Edinburgh; suc. to the Baronetcy, 21 Sep. 1753; was M.P. for Anstruther Easter Burghs (three
2 CONC  Paris.), 1766, till he resigned in 1782 ; and again 1790, till he resigned in 1793. He entailed all his estates, 18 Feb. 1778. He m. 4 Oct. 1750, at Edinburgh, Janet, da. of James Fall, of Dunbar, Merchant, sometime Provost and M
2 CONC .P. for that town, by Jean, da. of Patrick Murray, of Pennyland, in Caithness. He d. 4 July 1799, aged 80. Will pr. July 1799. His widow d. 17 Feb. 1802, aged 85. Will pr. 1802."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n405/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 387
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT √ Burke's Peerage - page 112 Volume 1 107th edition
2 CONT * 1e ''' Sir John Anstruther of that Ilk, 2nd Bt'''; b 27 Dec 1718; m 4 Oct 1750 Janet  (d 17 Feb 1802), dau of james Fall, of Dunbar, and d 4 July 1799, having had, with other issue; ...
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
