2 CONT "<strong>Sir Adam Inglis, Baronet [S 1687] of Cramond</strong>, 2nd but surviving son and heir, born 21 October 1714; admitted Advocate, 1736; studied the Law at Leyden University; succeeded to the Baronetcy, 3 March 1771. He died
2 CONC  22 November 1766, at Barnbougle castle, Dorothea, 2nd and youngest daughter of James (Primrose), 2nd Earl of Rosebery [S], by Mary, daughter of the Hon. John Campbell, of Mamore. He died s.p. at Cramond, 9 November 1772, aged 58.
2 CONC  She died at Bath, 3 December 1783."
2 CONT
