1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Thomas Stirling, Baronet [S. 1666], of Strowan</strong>, co. Perth, br. and h. male, b. Oct. 1733; served in the Dutch, 1747, and afterwards in the English service, being at the capture of Martinique in 1759 and of th
2 CONC e Havannah in 1762, and at the conquest of Canada, 1763. He served in the American war till 1780 when he was severely wounded; was sometime (1782) Col. of the 71st Foot and subsequently, 1790, of the 41st Foot, becoming full Gener
2 CONC al in 1801. He purchased the estate of Strowan in 179t, and suc. to the Baronetcy, 26 July 1799. He d at Strowan, unm., 8 May 1808, when the Baronetcy became extinct. Will pr. 1808."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n273/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 254
