1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GENERAL SIR ROBERT LAURIE OF MAXWELLTON baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/389/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 389]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Process of Divorce===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 February 1774: Process of Divorce - Major Robert Lawrie of the 7th or Queen's Regiment of Dragoons, only son of Sir Robert Lawrie of Maxwellton, baronet, against Elizabeth Maria Ruthven, now third daughter of James Lord Ruthv
2 CONC en, his spouse, married July 1763. Lieutenant Hatton Flood co-respondent. XIV. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso22scotuoft/page/49/mode/1up Consistorial Processes and Decreets: number 626 on p. 49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Robert Laurie, Baronet [1685], of Maxwelton</strong>, only s. and h. ; was M.P. for Dumfries-shire for 30 years (six Paris.) 1774 till his death in 1804 ; suc. to the Baronetcy, 28 April 1779 . entered early into the 
2 CONC Army ; was in 1779 Lient.-Col., 16th Light Dragoons ; Major-General in 1798, and finally, 1883, General ; Knight Marshal of Scotland 1785 till death. He m. firstly, 18 July 1763, at Edinburgh, Mary Elizabeth, da. of James (Ruthven
2 CONC ), Lord Ruthven of Freeland [8.], by his 2d wife Anne da. of James (Stewart), 2d Earl of Bute [S.]. She was living 1769. He m. secondly, at Ipswich, 25 April 1778, Judith, widow of Robert Wollaston, da. of ( — ) Hatley. He d. 10 S
2 CONC ep. 1804, at Dumfries. Admon. Jan. 1805. His widow, by whom he had no issue, d. 25 Jan. 1824, in Upper Seymour street, aged 76. Will pr. 1824."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n351/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 332
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1790-1820/member/laurie-sir-robert-1738-1804 The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1790-1820], ed. R. Thorne, 1986
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_Robert_Laurie,_5th_Baronet Wikipedia: Sir Robert Laurie, 5th Baronet]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Laurie, 5th Baronet (circa 1738 – 1804) was a Scottish soldier and politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1774 to 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurie was the only son of Sir Robert Laurie, 4th Baronet and his wife Christian Erskine, daughter of Charles Erskine, Lord Tinwald. He succeeded his father in the baronetcy on Wednesday, 28 April 1779.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the army in 1762 and was captain in the 71st Foot. In 1765 he was a captain in the 7th Dragoon Guards and in 1771 a major.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1774 general election he was returned as Member of Parliament for Dumfriesshire. Also in 1779 he became lieutenant-colonel in the 16th Light Dragoons and joint surveyor general of window and house tax in Scotland. He was re
2 CONC -elected MP for Dumfriesshire in 1780 and 1784. In 1785 he was appointed Knight Marischal of Scotland but lost his position as surveyor general of window and house tax in 1789. He was made full General in 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurie was extremely irregular in his attendance in Parliament, but retained his seat until his death on Monday, 10 September 1804. He had married firstly Elizabeth Maria Ruthven, daughter of James, 5th Lord Ruthven on Monday, 18 
2 CONC July 1763, with whom he had a son and a daughter. Having divorced his first wife in 1774, he had married secondly Judith Wollaston, daughter of Captain Hatley and widow of Robert Wollaston of Ipswich, Suffolk on Saturday, 25 April
2 CONC  1778. He was succeeded by his son Sir Robert Laurie, 6th Baronet.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092524408/page/n351/mode/2up?view=theater&q=Laurie Complete Baronetage 1665 to 1707 by George Edward Cokayne Volume 4 Published 1904 Page 332]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT V. 1779. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Laurie, Baronet [1685], of Maxwelton aforesaid, only son and heir; was M.P. for Dumfriesshire for 30 years (six Parliaments.) 1774 till his death in 1804; succeeded to the Baronetcy, Wednesday, 28 April 1779. entered ea
2 CONC rly into the Army; was in 1779 Lieutenant Colonel, 16th Light Dragoons; Major General in 1798, and finally, 1883, General; Knight Marshal of Scotland, 1785 till death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married firstly, Monday, 18 July 1763, at Edinburgh, Mary Elizabeth Ruthven , daughter of James Ruthven, Lord Ruthven of Freeland [S.], by his 2nd wife Anne Stewart, daughter of James Stewart, 2nd Earl of Bute [S.]. She was liv
2 CONC ing 1769. He married secondly, at Ipswich, Saturday, 25 April 1778, Judith Wollaston, widow of Robert Wollaston, daughter of ( — ) Hatley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died Monday, 10 September 1804, at Dumfries. Administration [of will] January 1805. His widow, by whom he had no issue, died Sunday, 25 January 1824, in Upper Seymour street, aged 76. Will proved 1824.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.scotlandspeople.gov.uk/search-records/church-registers/church-births-baptisms#form&record_type=opr_births&church_type=Old%20Parish%20Registers&surname=Laurie&surname_so=exact&forename_so=exact&from_year=1730&t
2 CONC o_year=1760&parent_names=Robert&parent_names_so=soundex&parent_name_two=Erskine&parent_name_two_so=soundex&sort=asc&order=Date&field=year Scotland's People: Old Parish Registers: Births and Baptisms] and [https://www.familysearch.
2 CONC org/ark:/61903/1:1:XYHV-RVZ FamilySearch: Robert Baronet Laurie in entry for Robert Baronet Laurie, "Scotland Births and Baptisms, 1564-1950"]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 26 July 1745 birth or baptism of Robert Laurie, Baronet, son of Robert Laurie, Baronet, and Christian Erskine [child 5], in the parish of Dumfries
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.scotlandspeople.gov.uk/search-records/church-registers/church-banns-marriages#form&record_type=opr_marriages&church_type=Old%20Parish%20Registers&surname=Laurie&surname_so=exact&forename=Robert&forename_so=exa
2 CONC ct&spouse_name=Elizabeth%20Maria%20Ruthven&spouse_name_so=exact&from_year=1745&to_year=1804&sort=asc&order=Date&field=year Scotland's People: Old Parish Records - Marriages and Banns] and  [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/
2 CONC 1:1:XYWN-YQ3 FamilySearch: Robert Baronet Laurie in entry for Robert Baronet Laurie, "Scotland Marriages, 1561-1910"]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 17 July 1763 marriage or banns of Robert Laurie, Baronet to Elizabeth Maria Ruthven, in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.scotlandspeople.gov.uk/search-records/church-registers/church-births-baptisms#form&record_type=opr_births&church_type=Old%20Parish%20Registers&surname=Laurie&surname_so=soundex&forename_so=exact&from_year=1763
2 CONC &to_year=1780&parent_names=Robert&parent_names_so=exact&parent_name_two=Ruthven&parent_name_two_so=soundex Scotland's People: Old Parish Registers: Births and Baptisms] NOTE: can only find one child born in Scotland'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible list of 1 child of Robert Laurie and Elizabeth Ruthven from first: 13 June 1769 Anne Wortely Mo Laurie
2 CONT
