1 NAME Midshipman Robert Pitcairn (Royal Navy)
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Died at Sea; Body never recovered
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 MAY 1752
2 ADDR
3 CITY Burntisland
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1770
2 PLAC Lost at Sea aboard the HMS Auroroa
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A memorial dedicated at Find-a-Grave #9288829
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT British Naval Officer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As a Midshipman on the HMS Swallow, he discovered Pitcairn Island on July 3, 1767. It was named in his honor by Captain Philip Carteret, the Swallow's commander. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Trying to pinpoint the site without a chronometer, Carteret charted the island 188 nautical miles west of its actual location; this miscalculation would lead Fletcher Christian and the mutineers of the Bounty to settle there in 17
2 CONC 90.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pitcairn himself did not live to see how famous his little island would become. On December 29, 1769, the 17 year-old discoverer set sail aboard the HMS Aurora on a voyage from the Cape of Good Hope to India. Neither the Aurora no
2 CONC r its crew were ever seen again, and it was assumed that the ship went down in a storm in the Indian Ocean.
