1 SOUR
2 DATA
3 DATE 29 APR 2020
3 TEXT Birth Surname
3 TEXT lexander Montgomerie, 10th Earl of Eglinton (10 February 1723 – 25 October 1769), was a Scottish peer.
4 CONT
4 CONT Eglinton was the son of the 9th Earl of Eglinton. His mother and third wife of the 9th Earl was Susanna Montgomery, Countess of Eglinton the renowned society beauty. He was the Grand Master Mason of the Grand Lodge of Scotland fro
4 CONC m 1750-51.
4 CONT
4 CONT Alexander planned and built the conservation village of Eaglesham, Scotland in 1769 around the basic plan of a capital 'A'. The Earl introduced the young James Boswell to the joys of London society in the early 1760s, and figures 
4 CONC prominently in Boswells London Journal, 1762-63.
4 CONT
4 CONT The Earl was shot on the beach near his own estate of Ardrossan by an excise officer or Gaudger (Scots) named Mungo Campbell on 24 October 1769 following a dispute about the latter's right to bear arms on the Earl's grounds.[1] Th
4 CONC e Earl died from his abdominal wounds.[2] late that evening. Campbell was convicted of murder but died by his own hand before the sentence could be carried out.[3]
4 CONT
4 CONT References[edit]
4 CONT Jump up ^ The Trial of Mungo Campbell for the Murder of Alexander Earl of Eglintoun. (1770). London. Page 2
4 CONT Jump up ^ The Trial of Mungo Campbell, page 3, D. Wilson & G. Nicol (publ.); London: 1770
4 CONT Jump up ^ Account of the murder of the 10th Earl of Eglinton
2 OBJE
