1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note by Ed Wyse on January 16, 2011: It is difficult to resolve these references to Earls of Northesk.  If David, Earl of Northesk, is father of Margaret Carnegie then it implies that his name is David Carnegie.  L
2 CONC ater, George, Second Earl of Northesk, marries Lady Anne.  One possible explanation, which is a bit of a stretch, is that David, who may have been named David Carnegie, was not the Fourth Earl of Northesk, but the First and his so
2 CONC n, George, who also may have been named Carnegie, would have been the Second Earl of Northesk.
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************************************************************************************************** http://books.google.com/books?id=lyENAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA367#v=onepage&q=&f=false Page 367
2 CONT
2 CONT “   I. George, Lord Balgonie and Raith, who died before his father, in August 1721, having married in 1716 his cousin-german, Lady Margaret Carnegie, eldest daughter of David, fourth Earl of Northesk, by Lady Margaret Wemyss, seco
2 CONC nd daughter of Margaret, Countess of Wemyss..."
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************************************************************************************************** http://books.google.com/books?id=lyENAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA368#v=onepage&q=&f=false Page 368
2 CONT
2 CONT “   II. Lady Anne, married to George, second Earl of Northesk."
