2 CONC cond Earl of Northesk, marries Lady Anne.  One possible explanation, which is a bit of a stretch, is that David, who may have been named David Carnegie, was not the Fourth Earl of Northesk, but the First and his son, George, who a
2 CONC lso may have been named Carnegie, would have been the Second Earl of Northesk.
