1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Wemyss, 5th Earl of Wemyss (30 August 1699 – 21 March 1756) was the son of David Wemyss, 4th Earl of Wemyss.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 17 September 1720, he married Janet Charteris, heiress of the great Colonel Francis Charteris, and they had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # David Wemyss, 6th Earl of Wemyss (1721–1787)
2 CONT # Francis Charteris, 7th Earl of Wemyss (1723–1808)
2 CONT # James Wemyss (1726–1786)
2 CONT # Frances Wemyss (d. 1789)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1730, he was key to securing the release his father-in-law from Newgate Prison after he was sentenced to hang for the capital felony of rape.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second son, Francis, the seventh Earl, legally changed his name to Charteris, his mother's maiden name, on his inheritance of Colonel Charteris's estates and fortune built upon gambling.
2 CONT
