1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Aston,_5th_Lord_Aston_of_Forfar James Aston, 5th Lord Aston of Forfar] (23 May 1723 – 24 August 1751) was a son of Walter Aston, 4th Lord Aston of Forfar, and Lady Mary Howard.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 30, 1742, James married Lady Barbara Talbot, sister of the 14th Earl of Shrewsbury, by whom he had two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1748, he succeeded his father as Lord Aston of Forfar in the Peerage of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Aston produced no direct male heir by the time of his death in 1751, when his title passed to his distant cousin Philip Aston, 6th Lord Aston of Forfar.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'James Aston, 5th Lord Aston of Forfar', Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, 1 April 2013, 02:12 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Aston,_5th_Lord_Aston_of_Forfar&oldid=548079664>
2 CONC  [accessed 18 November 2013]
