2 CONT
2 CONT Élisabeth Philippine Marie Hélène de France[1], Fille de France (Daughter of France), known as Madame Élisabeth, (3 May 1764 – 10 May 1794), was the youngest sister of King Louis XVI of France. Having lived through the French Revo
2 CONC lution beside the king and his family, she was executed during the Reign of Terror in Paris. Contents [show]
2 CONT
