1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Anne Campbell'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://thepeerage.com/p3142.htm#i31413
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Campbell married Matthew Fortescue, 2nd Baron Fortescue of Castle Hill, son of Hugh Fortescue and Hon. Lucy Aylmer, on 8 July 1752.1 She died on 26 May 1812.4
2 CONT      She was the daughter of John Campbell of Cawdor and Mary Pryse.3 As a result of her marriage, Anne Campbell was styled as Baroness Fortescue of Castle Hill on 8 July 1752. From 8 July 1752, her married name became Fortescue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne Campbell and Matthew Fortescue, 2nd Baron Fortescue of Castle Hill
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Hugh Fortescue, 1st Earl Fortescue+3 b. 12 Mar 1753, d. 16 Jun 1841
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Captain Hon. Matthew Fortescue+3 b. 12 Apr 1754, d. 19 Nov 1842
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 729. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pee
2 CONC rage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.[S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family."
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1473.
