1 OCCU 4th Marquess of Lothian, 6th Earl of Ancrame, 5th Earl of Lothian, 4th Earl of Ancram, 4th Viscount of Briene, 7th Lord Jedburgh, Knight of the Thistle
1 TITL General
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===William Henry Kerr===
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born in 1710. He was the son of '''William Kerr 3rd Marquess of Lothian''' and '''Margaret Nicolson'''. He died on 12 April 1775.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Marquess of Lothian [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 6th Earl of Ancrame [S.1633] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 5th Earl of Lothian [S.1631] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Earl of Ancram [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Viscount of Briene [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 7th Lord Jedburgh [S.1622] on 28 July 1767
2 CONT He succeeded as the 6th Lord Kerr of Nisbet [S.1633] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 6th Lord Kerr of Langnewtoun [S.1633] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 6th Lord Kerr of Dolphinstoun [S.1633] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 5th Lord Ker of Newbattle [S.1631] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Lord Ker of Newbottle [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Lord Ker of Oxnam [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Lord Ker of Jedburgh [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Lord Ker of Dolphinstoun [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He succeeded as the 4th Lord Ker of Nisbet [S.1701] on 28 July 1767.
2 CONT He was appointed Knight - Order of the Thistle (K.T.) in 1768.
2 CONT He was appointed Representative Peer - Scotland 1768-1774.
2 CONT He was Aide-de-Camp to the Duke of Cumberland in 1745/46. 
2 CONT He gained the rank of Cornet in 1735. 
2 CONT He gained the rank of Captain in the 11th Foot in 1739.
2 CONT He gained the rank of Captain in the 1st Foot Guards in 1741.
2 CONT He gained the rank of Colonel of the 24th Foot between 1747 and 1752.
2 CONT He gained the rank of Colonel of the 11th Dragoons between 1752-1775.
2 CONT He gained the rank of Major-General in 1755.
2 CONT He gained the rank of Lieutenant-General in 1758.
2 CONT He gained the rank of General in 1770.
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Fontenoy in 1745, where he was wounded.
2 CONT He fought in the Battle of Culloden where he commanded cavalry in 1746. 
2 CONT He was a Member of Parliament (M.P.-Whig) for Richmond Yorkshire in 1747-1763.  
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 November 1735 at St. James's, Westminster, London, England he married '''Lady Caroline Darcy''' daughter of '''Robert Darcy 3rd Earl of Holderness''' and '''Lady Frederica Susanna Schomberg'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of William & Caroline:'''
2 CONT General William John Kerr, 5th Marquess of Lothian (13 Mar 1737-4 Jan 1815)
2 CONT Lady Louisa Kerr (1738-1830)
2 CONT Lady Wilhelmina Frances Kerr (b.1759)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p1199.htm
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Kerr,_4th_Marquess_of_Lothian
2 CONT
