1 NAME William /Ross/
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Ross
2 _MARNM Ross
1 NAME William Ross 14th Lord Ross of Halkhead & 17th of Balnagown
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 2 JUN 1718
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 AUG 1754
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Ross was not descended from the Rosses of Blanagown. He was descended from the Lord Ross of Halkhead family. These were genetically two different families.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Rosses of Balnagown were a descendant branch of the original Earls of Ross. The Halkhead Rosses are thought to be descended from the men who came from the town of Ros in Normandy with William the Conqueror.
2 CONT
2 CONT The descendants of the original Earls held Balnagown, and were chiefs of Clan Ross, since losing the Earldom circa 1372. 
2 CONT
2 CONT George 11th Lord Ross of Halkhead attempted to assert himself as Chief of Clan Ross, the larger goal being a claim to the recently extinct Earldom of Ross.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1676, The Clan was unhappy with their Chief, [https://www.geni.com/people/David-Ross-13th-of-Balnagowan/6000000010841955621 David Ross 13th of Balnagown]. Lord Ross saw this an opportunity and made promises to David 13th of Bal
2 CONC nagown to advance the interests of all who bore the Ross name in exchange for the title of Chief.
2 CONT
2 CONT On top of this trouble with the Clan, David 13th of Balnagown was also faced with crippling debt due to his father's investment in war & a lack of male heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around the year 1694, the son of George 11th Lord Ross of Halkhead, William 12th Lord Ross of Halkhead, took this opportunity to claim a relationship with the Rosses of Balnagown and began a campaign to become successor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded & in an agreement dated 22 Jul 1706 William's brother Charles became 14th of Balnagown. After Charles's death in 1732, he was buried in Fearn Abbey, which was both founded by & the burial place of Ferquhard MacTaggart
2 CONC , even though there was no relation, at least not on his patrilineal line.
2 CONT
2 CONT William's son George then became 13th Lord Ross of Halkhead & 16th of Balnagown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources===
2 CONT
