2 CONT William the 8th Earl was in the Army in 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served on the Continent and in 1745 joined Sir John COPE at Dunbar and was present at the BATTLE OF PRESTONPANS in 1745. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He then took command of the Glasgow Regiment and joined the English Army at Stirling.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1757 he was Governor of Gibraltar being at that time a Lieutenant-General of Artillery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died while in Gibraltar.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had no issue so the Earldom was inherited by one of his younger brothers who was a priest in the Church of England, the intervening brothers having died before Sir William.
