1 NAME Alexander /Home/ Earl of Home
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Home
2 NSFX Earl of Home
2 _MARNM Home
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 OCT 1786
1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}    Sir Alexander HOME, 9th Earl of HOME inherited the title from his older brother Sir William HOME 8th Earl of HOME who had no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Before inheriting the title he had become a Clergyman in the Church of England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT    He married Marion HOME whose parents were James of Ayton, HOME and Janet HAIG.
2 CONT
2 CONT    They had one son, Sir Alexander HOME the t0th Earl. He inherited the title when he was just 17.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:   Burke's Peerage, page 1277
2 CONT
2 CONT 9th Earl of Home...
2 CONT
2 CONT Clergyman of the Church of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT    His eldest son, William, Lord DUNGLASS, an officer of the Coldstream Guards, was killed at the Battle of Gilford during the American Revolution, 1781, unmarried. He was succeeded by his second son, Alexander, as 10th Earl.
2 CONT
2 CONT    Alexander married Primrose ELPHINSTONE by whom he had William HOME, LORD DUNGLASS and Elizabeth Eleanora HOME.
2 CONT
2 CONT    He then married Marion HOME with whom he had Sir Alexander HOME, 10th Earl of HOME.
2 CONT
2 CONT    He then married Abigail Brown RAMEY with whom he had two daughters, Caroline and Sophie Charlotte.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Alexander died before the 28th April 1761 so he did not inherit the title from his older brother William.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [The Peerage] http://www.thepeerage.com/p7990.htm#i79899
