2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Mackenzie, James Stuart-</strong>. ?-06/04/1800. Ref: 1461. Male.
2 CONT * Titles and British Honours: Rt Hon PC.
2 CONT * Profession: Landowner, Politician.
2 CONT * Appointments Held: MP 1742-7 Argyllshire, 1747-54 Buteshire, 1854-61 Ayr Burghs, 1761-80 Ross-shire; Envoy Extraordinary 1758-61 to the King of Sardinia; Lord Privy Seal of Scotland 1763-1800.
2 CONT * Schools and Tutors: Eton College, Buckinghamshire 1728-32.
2 CONT * Undergraduate Studies: Leyden 1737.
2 CONT * Mother: Lady Anne Campbell.
2 CONT * Father: James Stuart, 2nd. Earl of Bute.
2 CONT * Siblings: John Stuart, 3rd Earl of Bute FRSE 1713-92.
2 CONT * Other Family: Brother-in-law of Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet FRSE 1718-85.
2 CONT * References: Shapin 311.
2 CONT * Memberships: FSA(Scot).
2 CONT * Date of Election: 17/11/1783.
2 CONT * Proposers: Founder Member.
2 CONT * Notes: Born c1717.
2 CONT * Fellow Type: OF.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Waterston, Charles D; Macmillan Shearer, A (July 2006). [http://www.royalsoced.org.uk/cms/files/fellows/biographical_index/fells_indexp2.pdf Biographical index of former fellows of the Royal Society of Edinburgh, 1783-200
2 CONC 2]: Biographical Index. II. Edinburgh: The Royal Society of Edinburgh. ISBN 978-0-902198-84-5. page 592
2 CONT
