1 NAME Field Marshal John Henry Campbell, 5th Duke of Argyll
1 SEX M
1 BAPM
2 DATE JUN 1723
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 JUN 1723
2 PLAC Inverary castle, Argyll, , Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 MAY 1806
2 PLAC Inverary Castle, Argyleshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 10 JUN 1806
2 PLAC Collegiate Church, Kilmun, Cowal, Argyllshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Duke of Argyll
1 TITL Field Marshal
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John succeeded his father in 1770, became the first President of the Highland Society of Scotland and married a celebrated beauty, Elizabeth Gunning, widow of the sixth Duke of Hamilton, in 1759. Both Duke and Duch
2 CONC ess were subscribers to Robert Burns' Poems.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burns arrived at Inverary in June 1787, when the Duke of Argyll had a large house party. The inn keeper was too busy attending to the Duke's guests to have time for passing travellers. Burns is supposed to have scrawled his 'On In
2 CONC civility shown him at Inverary' on one of the inn windows:
2 CONT
2 CONT     "Whoe'er he be that sojourns here,
2 CONT
2 CONT     I pity much his case —
2 CONT
2 CONT     Unless he come to wait upon
2 CONT
