1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Archibald Edmondstone of Duntreath</strong>, co. Stirling, Esq., 1st s. and h. of Archibald Bdmonstone of Duntreath aforesaid, and of Red Hall, co. Antrim, by his 2d wife Anne (m. 1716), sister of John, 4th Duke op Argyll
2 CONC  [S.], da. of the Hon. John Campbell, of Mamore, was b. 10 Oct. 1717, at Silver Banks, in oo. Dumbarton ; admitted to the Middle Temple, 5 Dec. 1737; was M.P. for Dumbartonshire (three Paris.), 1761-80; for Ayr burghs (two Paris )
2 CONC , 1780-90, and for Dumbartonshire, again, 1790-96, being cr. a Baronet, 20 May 1774. He m. firstly, in or before 1762, Susanna Mary, da. of Roger and sister of Benjamin Harene, of Pootscray place, Kent. She d. 4 and was bur. 11 Ap
2 CONC ril 1776, at St. Marylebone. He m. secondly, 28 April 1778, at St. Geo. Han. sq., Hester, 2d da. of Sir John Heathcote, 2d Baronet [1733], of Normanton, by Bridget, da. of Thomas White. She d. s.p. 1796. He d. 20 July 1807, aged 8
2 CONC 9. Will pr. 1807."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524416#page/n193/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1906; Vol. V; page 170
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald, 11th of Duntreath, 1768-1807. (b.1717) 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Created a Baronet of the United Kingdom, 3rd May 1774 )
2 CONT
2 CONT For many years M.O. for Dumbarton (also for Ayr and Irvine).
2 CONT
2 CONT m.1stly, in 1753, Susanna Mary, dau.of French gentleman, Roger Harene, and by
2 CONT
2 CONT     her (who died in 1776) had 5 sons & 3 daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT     1  Archibald b.1754. He had a military education on the Continent and then because a Lieut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT         in the 1st Regiment of Foodguards. Was A.D.C. to General Riedsel (Commander of 
2 CONT
2 CONT         German division of army under General burgoyne) in the campaign in the American War
2 CONT
2 CONT         of Inderpendence which ended with the surrender at Saratoge in 1777. Returning, he 
2 CONT
2 CONT         died of consuption in 1780, aged only 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT     2  William Archibald, Civil Servant in India, died in Calcutta, 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT     3  Charles, 2nd Bt., b. 1764. (See below)
2 CONT
2 CONT     4  George b.1764. Vicar of Pollerne.
2 CONT
2 CONT     5  Neil Benjamin, b. 1765. Went as a young man to India & rose to second most important
2 CONT
2 CONT         post in Civil Service. m.1803 Charlotte Anne, dau. of Philip Friell, by whom he had 
2 CONT
2 CONT         5 sons & 6 daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT            (1)  William Archibald, b.1804, died in India, 1827.
2 CONT
2 CONT            (2)  Neil Benjamin, b.1809, m. Madeline Elinor, only dau. of  W.H. Trant 
2 CONT
2 CONT                   of Drumonethy, Co. Limerick, by whom he had 2 sons, 
2 CONT
2 CONT                   -1 Neil Benjamin (b.1883)
2 CONT
2 CONT                   -2 William Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (3) Charles Welland, b.1811. Took Holy Orders. 
2 CONT
2 CONT               m. Susan Mary D'Oyley dau.of Rev. Philip Douglas, by whom he had 
2 CONT
2 CONT                    (1) Susan Carnegie (b.1844).
2 CONT
2 CONT                    ( )  Other daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (4) George Frederick, b.1813, 
2 CONT
2 CONT               m. Anne Farly, dau. of Mr. Turner of Bengal Civil Service, 
2 CONT
2 CONT                    and had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT         (5) James Harene, b.1820, d.1834.
2 CONT
2 CONT     The daughters of Neil Benjamin (b.1765) were:
2 CONT
2 CONT         (1) Charlotte Anne, 
2 CONT
2 CONT               m.1st, James Carnegie Bengal Civil Service, who died in 1831, 
2 CONT
2 CONT               m. 2nd, the Rev. J. Hodgson, Vicar of St Peter's Isle of Thanet.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (2) Henrietta Dashwood.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (3) Suanna, m. the Rev.Thomas Lumsden of Cushnie, Aberdeenshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (4) Louisa MacLeod, m. the Rev Thomas Clement Browne & had children.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (5) Anne Craigie.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (6) Alicia Augusta.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 3 daughters of Sir Archibald were:-
2 CONT
2 CONT     1  Susanne Margaret, m. James Trevithick of Addington Park, Surrey by whom
2 CONT
2 CONT         she had 2 sons & 4 daughters. The son where:
2 CONT
2 CONT         (1) Barton, b.1779, m. Eliza, dau. of the Rev. John Strachey, by whom he had a 
2 CONT
2 CONT              dau., 
2 CONT
2 CONT              -1 Eliza, m. her cousin Leonard Strachey, and they had children.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (2) James, b.1797, d.1849.
2 CONT
2 CONT         Their 4 daughters, all died unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT     2  Anne Mary, m. Major-General Henry Read of Crowood, Wilts, by whom she had 
2 CONT
2 CONT         two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT         (1) Mary Anne, m. J. Richmond Seymour of Inholmes, Wilts. They had 3 sons 
2 CONT
2 CONT               & 3 daughters. The sons where:
2 CONT
2 CONT                -1 Henry Richmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT               -2 Charles Frederick.
2 CONT
2 CONT               -3 George.
2 CONT
2 CONT               The daughters were:
2 CONT
2 CONT               -1 Alithea Emma.
2 CONT
2 CONT               -2 Jane mary Susanna.
2 CONT
2 CONT               -3 Charlotte Isabella.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (2) Louisa.
2 CONT
2 CONT         (3) Sarah, who died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT m. 2ndly, Hester, dau. of Sir John Heathcote Bt. of Normanton Park, Rutland.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had no children. She died in 1797 & he died, aged 89, in 1807
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his 3rd son.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.edmonstone.com/
