2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Wolfe Murray, Lord Cringletie</strong>, a Senator of the College of Justice in Scotland, godson of Gen. Wolfe, b. 5 Jan. 1759; m. 7 April, Isabella Katherine, only dau. of James Charles Edward Stuart Strange, Esq. (
2 CONC godson of Prince Charles Edward Stuart), H.E.I.C., by Margaret his wife, dau. of James Durham, of Largo, Fife, and by her (who d. 25 Dec. 1847) had issue...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Lord Cringletie d. 29 May, 1836."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera02byuburk#page/1144/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry of Great Britain & Ireland], Vol. II, page 1144
2 CONT
2 CONT "(352) <strong>James Wolfe Murray of Cringletie</strong>, bom 5th January 1759; died 29th May 1836. He was named after the hero of Quebec, and became a Lord of Session as Lord Cringletie. He married, 7th April 1807, Isabella, daug
2 CONC hter of J. C. E. S. Strange, who died 25th December 1847. They had issue :-
2 CONT
2 CONT * James (No. 353).
2 CONT * Colonel Alexander Murray, died s.p. 24th December 1865. Married, 1853, Eugenia, daughter of Colonel Curtis.
2 CONT * Major-General Thomas Andrew Lumsden Murray, born 1st March 1825 ; died 3rd October 1893. He married, 1849, Elizabeth, daughter of John Charlton Fisher, LL.D., Canada, who died 10th November 1906, having had:
2 CONT ** Thomas Murray, died s.p.
2 CONT ** Dennistoun Murray, died s.p.
2 CONT * Philip Charles Murray, died 1842."
2 CONT
