1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Francis, ninth Earl of Moray</strong>, was born 11 January 1737. As a young man he completed his education by foreign travel, and seems to have made excellent use of the opportunities afforded him. On his succession to th
2 CONC e title and the family estates he paid great attention to the development of the latter, and became celebrated as a tree-planter. Within two years after his succession it is said he planted at Darnaway, Doune, and Donibristle upwa
2 CONC rds of thirteen million trees, of which nearly a million and a half were oaks. The Earl sat as a Representative Peer from 1784 to 1796, and was on 4 June 1796 created BARON STUART OF CASTLE STUART in the county of Inverness, in th
2 CONC e Peerage of Great Britain. He was Lord-Lieutenant of Morayshire. He died at Drumsheugh, near Edinburgh, 28 August 1810, aged seventy-three, and was buried at Donibristle. He married, at Gray, 28 June 1763, Jane, eldest daughter o
2 CONC f John, twelfth Lord Gray, and by her, who died 19 February 1786, had issue : 
2 CONT * James, Lord Doune, born at Edinburgh, 2 March 1765, died v.p. at Bath 11 June 1776. 
2 CONT * John, also styled Lord Doune after his brother's death, was born at Edinburgh 11 February 1768 ; elected M.P. for Great Bedwin 1790 ; died, v.p. unmarried, at Drumsheugh, 6 July 1791, and was buried at Donibristle. 
2 CONT * Francis, tenth Earl of Moray. 
2 CONT * Archibald, twin with Francis, born at Edinburgh 2 February 1771 ; cornet 2nd Dragoon Guards 4 August 1790, and afterwards lieutenant-colonel of the Dorsetshire Militia. He died 30 October 1832, having married, 17 March 1793, Cor
2 CONC nelia, youngest daughter of Edmund Morton Pleydell of Melbourne St. Andrew, co. Dorset. By her, who died 1 March 1830, he left issue : 
2 CONT ** Francis Archibald, born 5 December 1793 ; died, unmarried, 14 July 1875. 
2 CONT ** John Morton, born 20 April 1795 ; died, unmarried, 6 July 1840. 
2 CONT ** James William, born 21 February 1797 ; died, unmarried, 2 December 1850. 
2 CONT ** Edmund Luttrell, born 21 February 1798 ; was rector of the parish of Winterborne Hough ton, co. Dorset; died 5 November 1869, having married, 2 September 1834, Elizabeth, second daughter of the Rev. J. L. Jackson, rector of Swa
2 CONC nage. She died 28 March 1885, leaving issue : 
2 CONT *** Edmund Archibald, fifteenth Earl, 
2 CONT *** Francis James, sixteenth Earl. 
2 CONT *** Morton Gray Stuart Gray, of Kinfauns Castle, co. Perth, and Gray House, co. Forfar. Born 16 April 1855. He and his sister received a Patent of Precedence 10 April 1897 as son and daughter of an Earl. In 1901 he assumed the add
2 CONC itional name and arms of Gray; married, 17 December 1890, Edith Douglas, daughter of Rear- Admiral George Palmer, and has issue : 
2 CONT **** Francis Douglas, born 10 July 1892. 
2 CONT **** Archibald John Morton, born 14 November 1894. 
2 CONT **** James Gray, born 9 February 1897. 
2 CONT **** Hermione Moray, born 13 October 1899. 
2 CONT *** Cornelia, married, 29 July 1873, to the Rev. William Henry Augustus Truell, of Clonmannon, co. Wicklow, and has issue. 
2 CONT ** Douglas Wynne, born 8 May 1801 ; died 10 December 1855, having married, 4 February 1842, Marcia, youngest daughter of Francis Fownes Luttrell. She died 13 February 1870, leaving issue a son, 
2 CONT *** Douglas Moray, born 22 January 1843 ; died, unmarried, 26 November 1863. 
2 CONT ** George Gray, born 20 April 1805; in holy orders; died, unmarried, 11 June 1835. 
2 CONT * Charles, died unmarried. 
2 CONT * Grace, married, 10 July 1789, to George Douglas of Cavers, and died March 1846. 
2 CONT * Anne, died 18 April 1837, aged fifty-six."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/326/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VI, page 326
