1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/MacQueen-282
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev Daniel MacQueen
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile managers: Robert Ledger and Noelene Ahern
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Maqueen, son of Rev Daniel Maqueen, min. of St. Giles, Edinburgh and Elizabeth Nisbet, was baptized on 29 May 1743 in Stirling, Stirling, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Universiy of Edinburgh, licensed by Presb,. of Edinburgh 26 Jun 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Reverend of Prestonkirk, East Lothian, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Mcqueen, son of Daniel McQueen, married Elizabeth Lyon on 10 Nov 1768 in Saint Cuthberts, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland.[3] She died 7 Jul 1773. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Janet, b 16 Jun 1769, d 13 Jul 1770
2 CONT     Elizabeth (Macqueen) Wilkie, b 9 Jun 1770, marr William Wilkie
2 CONT     Janet, b 9 Sep 1771 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel married Mary Lothian 2 Jan 1775. She died 11 Jun 1815. They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Margaret Macqueen, b 4 Oct 1775, mar Robet Moore, d abt 1810
2 CONT     Warburton, b 11 May 1777, d 15 Feb 1778
2 CONT     Mary Macqueen, b 1 Aug 1778, married Archibald Dunlope on 27 Dec 1805 in South Leith, Midlothian, Scotland.
2 CONT     Andrew MacQueen, Lieut Col 36th N. I., b 12 Dec 1780, baptized on 31 Dec 1780 in Prestonkirk, East Lothian, Scotland[5], d 26 Sep 1829
2 CONT     Daniel, b 12 Aug 1782 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 18 Jul 1808. 
