1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duncan Macpherson (1748-1817) continued his education on the continent, and had become a captain in the British army by the time he was 23, eventually serving with the 63rd Regiment of Foot in the American War of I
2 CONC ndependence. Whilst in North America he joined the 71st Fraser Highlanders as a major in 1776, rising to Lieutenant-Colonel and participating in several battles. On returning to Britain in 1781, he was captured by an American priv
2 CONC ateer and spent 16 months as a prisoner-of-war in New England before returning home.
2 CONT
2 CONT An Act of Parliament in 1784 restored Colonel Duncan MacPherson to the estates of his father. At the age of 50 he married a second cousin, Catherine Cameron, and they had four sons and four daughters together.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 27th Chief, Lt.Colonel, 3rd Regt Guards
