1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=124653671-2-7727&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-04c57c6ea280bb38c4fca9c054f2f4fa&mrid=f703d1add253feb6171a6f
2 CONC e7d6781398 MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 22 2016, 2:21:22 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Samuel Boone Grant  Birth 26 Nov 1762  Rowan County, North Carolina, USA Death 13 Aug 1789 (aged 26)  Switzerland County, Indiana, USA Burial  Grant Family Cemetery  Grant, Kenton County, Kentucky, USA  "Samuel Boone Grant
2 CONC , born 26 Nov., 1762, in North Carolina; died 13 Aug., 1789, near the Ohio River, in Indiana. Married Lydia Craig, daughter of Rev. Elijah Craig of Scott Co., Ky. Samuel Grant was killed by Indians on Grant's Lick Creek in Indiana
2 CONC , at the same time that his brother Moses was. He was thought, by his nephew, Col Samuel Moseby Grant, to have been a Captain under Col. Robert Johnson who led the expedition over the Ohio, which ended disastrously for Moses and S
2 CONC amuel Grant. Children : Elijah Grant, mentioned in his grandfather's will. Elizabeth Grant, mentioned in her frandfather's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Refernces: Draper Mss. 22 S 230-38. Draper Mss. 22 C 46." The Boone Family: A Genealogical History of the Descendants of George and ... De Hazel Atterbury Spraker,Jesse Procter Crump
2 CONT
2 CONT His body was removed from Ohio and buried in the family plot in Kenton.
