1 NAME Captain Kenneth Mackenzie, 8th of Redcastle
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 FEB 1748
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1789
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "VIII. <strong>Captan Kenneth Mackenzie, eighth of Redcastle</strong>. He was born on the 21st of February, 1748, and married at Edinburgh, on the 17th of August, 1767, Jean, daughter of James Thomson, Accountant-General of Excise
2 CONC  in Scotland, with issue — 
2 CONT * Roderick, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * Hector, who married at Edinburgh, on the 29th of March, 1800, Diana Davidson, daughter of Dr Davidson, of the H.E.I.C.S., Leeds, with issue — Robert Davidson Mackenzie, Adjutant 1st Bombay Light Cavalry, who died of cholera on t
2 CONC he 22nd of December, 1822, at Sholapore, India, without issue. She died at Garlieston in 1852. 
2 CONT * Boyd, who married William MacCall of Newlon-Stewart, without issue. 
2 CONT * Hanna, who was the last surviving- child of Kenneth, of Redcastle, married William MacCa, of Barnshalloch, and died at Creebridge, Newton-Stewart, on the 8th of August, 1849, aged 83 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Kenneth was tried for the murder of Kenneth Mackenzie, alias Jefferson. He was found guilty and sentenced to be hanged, but was afterwards pardoned. He divorced his wife ; went abroad ; entered the Russian service; and was
2 CONC  killed in 1789 near Constantinople, where he was Assistant Consul, in a duel with Captain Smith, master of a merchant ship, to whom he had entrusted all his property when he had got into trouble about Jefferson. He figures in Kay
2 CONC 's Edinburgh portraits as one of the Bucks of the City. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmackenz00mack#page/542/mode/2up History of the Mackenzies, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1894; page 542
