1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://digital.nls.uk/histories-of-scottish-families/archive/96684440?mode=transcription
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/historyofmacken00mack/page/540/mode/2up?q=541
2 CONT
2 CONT The second son, '''ALEXANDER MACKENZIE''', was born in 1772, and married in 1795, Helen, daughter of John Donaldson, Dunfermline, factor for the Earl of Dundonald, with issue — 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) William, who was born in 1797 and died in infancy ; 
2 CONT (2) 'John DONALDSON MACKENZIE', surgeon, who was born in 1803, and practised his profession in Jersey. He married, in 1840, Emma Caroline, daughter of John Landseer, and sister of the eminent painter, Sir Edwin Landseer,  with iss
2 CONC ue — Edwin John Landseer Mackenzie, of Kensington Park Gardens, London, who was born in 1843 ; and Landseer Mackenzie, of St. Bernard, Bournemouth, born in 1849. 
2 CONT (3) Alexander, who was born in 1806, and died young in 1822; 
2 CONT (4) David Donaldson, born in 181 1, and died unmarried in 1836; 
2 CONT (5) Margaret Donaldson, who was born in 1799, married James Symington, banker, and died in 1863, without surviving issue ; 
2 CONT (6) Helen, born in 1801, died in 1802 ; 
2 CONT (7) Mary Anne, born in 1808, and died young in 1823 ; and 
2 CONT (8) Jane Donaldson, who, in 1840, married Andrew Armstrong Kerr, banker, Edinburgh, with issue — Robert, who, born in 1843, became a Judge in Jamaica, married, with issue, and died in 1884; Alexander Charles, born in 1847, married
2 CONC , with issue; Andrew William, who, born in 1848, married, without issue; Henry Francis, born in 1855, married, with issue ; Frederick Ebenezer, born in 1858, and died in infancy. Helen Alexandrina, who married Francis Suther Melvi
2 CONC lle, Edinburgh, Depute Clerk of Session and Registrar of Law Agents in Scotland, with issue ; Jane ; and Margaret Jessie, who died young in 1868. William Mackenzie had also a daughter Margaret, who married (and died in 1832) John 
2 CONC Fraser of Honduras, with issue — a son, John, and a daughter, Catherine, who, in 1834, married William Napier, of Bathurst, New Brunswick, without issue. Alexander died in 1841.
