1 NAME George /Moir/ Min. of Peterhead
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Moir
2 NSFX Min. of Peterhead
2 _MARNM Moir
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Peterhead
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 APR 1741
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ellon
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 MAR 1818
1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 'The Rev' George Moir, M.A., took his degree of M.D. at Marischal College, Aberdeen ; diploma dated  1765 ; was, according to Scott's " Fasti," licensed 26th April, presented by George III., 6th May 1765, to Peterh
2 CONC ead, and ordained 11 th August following. Of this much respected gentleman, who was for the long period of fifty-five years minister of Peterhead, it is told that he had at the same place, at different times, " three churches,  th
2 CONC ree manses, and thrice an augmentation of his living." Dr. Moir had a sexton who lived in the Kirkton of Peterhead named Mutch, and he was fond of saying, "that there is Mutch in the Kirkton, but Moir (often pronounced More) in th
2 CONC e manse." He wrote " The Statistical Account of the Parish of Peterhead," which Is very valuable. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>George Moir</strong>, born 5th April 1741, son of Andrew M., min. of Ellon ; educated at Marischal College, Aberdeen, 1755-9 ; licen. by Presb. of Ellon 26th April, pres. by George in. 6th May, and ord. 11th Aug. 1763 ; M.
2 CONC D. (9th Sept. 1765); died 18th March 1818. In the course of his ministry he occupied the pulpits of three parish churches in Peterhead, that of the old church in the churchyard, 1763-70, that of the new church built on the Little 
2 CONC Links, 1770-1800, and afterwards that of the present church. He marr. 7th March 1766, Martha (died 17th Nov. 1816), third daugh. of Patrick Byres of Tonley, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Andrew, born 9th June 1767, died in East Indies in 1783; 
2 CONT * Patrick, Commissioner of the Court of Requests at Calcutta, born 26th June 1769, died 5th Feb. 1810 ; 
2 CONT * James, physician, born 11th Nov. 1770 ; 
2 CONT * Robert, born 23rd March 1772, died 28th March 1782 ; 
2 CONT * Janet, born 5th Nov. 1773 (marr. (1) 4th June 1792, Christopher Norton of Pinkridge : (2) Captain John Davidson, Gothenburg) ; 
2 CONT * John, artist, born 19th June 1775, died 28th Feb. 1857 ; 
2 CONT * William, Commissioner of Court of Requests, Calcutta, born 12th June 1777; 
2 CONT * George, born 21st May 1779, died 9th Oct. 1786; 
2 CONT * Forbes, born 16th March 1781, died 24th Feb. 1782; 
2 CONT * Jean, born 24th Feb. 1783 (marr. William Donald, min. of this parish) ; 
2 CONT * Andrew Robert, born 10th July 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc06scot#page/232/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VI, page 232
