1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes for George Warren McDannald: FAMILY STORY: A family legend tells of an Indian (Mohawk) attack on the frontier in Virginia in 1770, when George was 10 years old. Supposedly, Indians raided the McDannald farm a
2 CONC nd killed everyone they could find. George and his younger sister by 2 years, Jane, hid in a cattle trough. They were the sole survivors, and it is not known who raised the orphans or what became of Jane.
2 CONT
