2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben is buried in the McDannold Cemetery, Pike County, Missouri. There are 44 graves in the McDannold family cemetery. The cemetery was in use between the years 1840 to 1888. He attended the Grassy Lick Baptist Church for 60 yea
2 CONC rs. In December of 1835, he joined the Ramsey Creek Baptist Church. Reuben had been a deacon in Kentucky. Reuben was a large landowner near Aaron's Run, Montgomery County, Kentucky. The spelling of the last name was changed from M
2 CONC cDannald to McDannold in Mt. Sterling, Montgomery County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/w/a/l/Leila-Walsh-IA/PDFBOOK1.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT REUBEN MCDANNALD (ALEXANDER1) was born February 14, 1768 in Montgomery County, Kentucky (possibly Culpeper County, Virginia), and died August 14, 1854 in Paynesville, Pike County, Missouri. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married PHOEBE ELLIS August 12, 1790 in Montgomery County, Kentucky, daughter of WILLIAM ELLIS and AGNES CARR. She was born August 07, 1774 in Virginia, and died May 28, 1858 in Pike County, Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben emigrated to Kentucky at an early day, secured a large tract of land, which he improved with slave labor, and resided there until 1834, then sold out and emigrated to Pike county, Missouri, settled near Clarksville, bought 
2 CONC a farm and resided there until his death in 1854. John learned the trade of tanner and conducted the business in Owensville, Kentucky, and in connection with it engaged in the mercantile business. He resided there until his death 
2 CONC in 1834. He was a Whig in politics, and served several years as Sheriff of that county. Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben is buried in the McDannold Cemetery, Pike County, Missouri. There are 44 graves in the McDannold family cemetery. The cemetery was in use between the years 1840 to 1888. He attended the Grassy Lick Baptist Church for 60 yea
2 CONC rs. In December of 1835, he joined the Ramsey Creek Baptist Church. Reuben had been a deacon in Kentucky. Reuben was a large landowner near Aaron's Run, Montgomery County, Kentucky. The spelling of the last name was changed from M
2 CONC cDannald to McDannold in Mt. Sterling, Montgomery County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Reuben McDannald: Reuben emigrated from Montgomery Co., KY to Pike Co., Missouri inOct. 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Reuben McDannald: Burial: August 16, 1848, McDannold Cem., Pike Co., MO
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Phoebe Ellis: Phoebe was living with Sarah & Washington Treadway in the 1850 Pike Co., MO census.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Phoebe Ellis: Burial: May 30, 1858, McDannold Cem., Pike Co., MO
2 CONT
