2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond Co. NC Estate Recs. 1772-1933 CR082.508.15 - excerpted on p.56 of "Our Native Heath:
2 CONT
2 CONT "1827 - A descriptive list of the people who attended the personal estate sale of the dec'd Dr. Archibald Fairley: Neill McLean (weaver), Hugh McLean (piper), Giles McLean,, John Graham (Pike), John McNair (big), Mrs. Little (McNa
2 CONC ir's mother-in-law), Mr. Curry (at Archibald McRae's), Archibald McEachen (uncle), John Kelly (Marion), John McCole (one eye), Daniel McInnis (Capt.), James Huckabee (Marion), Peter Graham (Geo.), John McLaurin (big), Hugh McCole 
2 CONC (steady). Dr. Fairley left Eliza, his widow and two ch., Mary Ann and Effy Jane Fairley."
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Our Native Heath":
2 CONT
2 CONT "1842 January Term. The Petition of Alexander Malloy and wife Mary Ann Fairley, one of the children and heirs at law of Dr. Archibald Fairley, deceased...show that Dr. Fairley died possessed of sundry tracts of land in Richmond Co
2 CONC unty situated on the waters of Leaths Creek, of Gum Swamp and Lumber River. All of which lands have descended and come to your petitioner together with Effy Jane Fairley as tenants in common ... request is made to divide and appro
2 CONC priate lands between these two children ... J.B. Kelly & A.R. Kelly Attys for the Petitioners." - Estate Records CR 082.508.15
2 CONT
