1 NAME Margaret /McEachin/
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN McEachin
2 _MARNM Stewart
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Stewartsville Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Laurinburg
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 FEB 1783
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 MAR 1823
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=27092255
2 CONT
2 CONT From microfilm of the copy in the NC State Archives, in the Margaret Stewart - 1823" folder, from the "Richmond Co. Wills" boxes:
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the name of God Amen, I, Margaret Stewart, of Richmond Co. & State of NC, being of sound & perfect mind and memory (Blessed be God), do this 8th day of March in the year of our Lord 1823 make and publish this my last will and 
2 CONC testament in manner following, that is to say:
2 CONT
2 CONT First, I give and bequeath to my beloved daughter Mary Stewart one feather bed with all its furniture.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondly, I give & bequeath to my beloved son John Stewart, one feather bed with all its furniture.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thirdly, I give & bequeath to my beloved daughter Penelope Stewart one feather bed with all its furniture.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourthly, I give & bequeath to my brother-in-law John Stewart the sum of $10.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth, I give & bequeath to my beloved daughter Ann MacInnes 50 cents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sixth, I give & bequeath to my beloved daughter Margaret MacQueen 50 cents.
2 CONT
2 CONT I also authorise my Executors hereafter named to apply the sum of $60 for the purpose of placing two pair of decent tombstones at my deceased husband's grave & at my own.
2 CONT
2 CONT All the rest of my property, after paying my lawful debts & defraying my funeral expense, I wish to be equally divided between my 2 youngest daughters, Mary & Penelope.
2 CONT
2 CONT And thereby make & ordain my worthy friends Duncan McIntyre & John Carmichael Esquires, Executors of this my last will & testament. In witness whereof I, the said Margaret Stewart, have to this my last will & testament set my hand
2 CONC  & seal the day & year above written. {signed} Margaret Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed published & declared by the sd. Margaret Stewart the testatrix as her last will & testament in the presence of us who were present at the time of signing & sealing thereof. Archd Carmichael, Archd. C. Sinclair, Hugh 
2 CONC Carmichael.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond Co. April Term 1823, the written will was duly proven by Archd. Carmichael. Ordered to be Ordered to be recorded, Martin D. Sandford, CSC."
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravemarker reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Margaret, Consort of James Stewart and daughter of Patrick and Mary McEachin b. 2-3-1783, d. 3-18-1823"
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Patrick and Mary Fairley McEachin and the wife of James Stewart.
