1 NOTE According to Owen Clough (Genes Reunited), this George Gordon was the fifth Earl of Aboyne http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Gordon%2C_9th_Marquess_of_Huntly
2 CONT and had 3 boys and 3 girls with her, illegitimately. (He had 8 legitimate children with Catharine Cope.) Only George Eliot Elliott survived "childhood", emigrating to New Zealand and marrying Catharine Morne.  However, the 1841 ce
2 CONC nsus shows two Ann Eliotts born in 1796 and 1821 (bracketted together, indicating family tie) living in High Street, Swanage in the household of Robert Burt, 50, stonemason, with Laetitia his wife, the Burt children and Ann Manwel
2 CONC l [his mother-in-law]. Thus George's illegitimate daughter Ann survived until the age of 20.
