2 CONT "<STRONG>Alexander Clark</strong>, born 1703, son of James C, min. of the Tron Parish, Glasgow; M.A. (Glasgow, 17th Dec. 1727) ; held the office of Librarian 1727-31; licen. by Presb. of Glasgow 1st Sept. 1731 ; pres. by Thomas, E
2 CONC arl of Dundonald, and ord. 24th July 1733; died unmarr. 8th Sept. 1736. It was said of him that in his day there was "neither a minister nor preacher so accomplished in the West of Scotland." His sister, Lilias, was his executor."
2 CONT
