1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Johnson served as a Patriot in the American Revolution with the rank of Lieutenant from Pennsylvania. He served in the Frontier Rangers. [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/default.cfm H
2 CONC is DAR Ancestor # is: A063384.]
2 CONT *Further Information about the Frontier Rangers can be found at the following links:
2 CONT **https://claudiusboatman.wordpress.com/pa-revolutionary-service/
2 CONT **http://frontierrangers.blogspot.com/ From [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=29312960 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 6 2017, 6:49:09 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Peter and Mary (Phillips) Johnson.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that the stone has his year of death marked as 1828 but that his will was proven on April 13, 1818.  [https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.3.1/TH-1961-27615-15650-40?cc=1992421&wc=MCFT-Z3D:266278501,266530601 Two page will]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth and Richard were married in 1774 in Allegheny County, Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
