2 CONC build a house, and a tract of land to grow food. This information is all recorded in A LIST OF EARLY SETTLERS OF GEORGIA. On June 15, 1733 a ship left London and arrived in Savannah August 29,1733. According to a publication by Sa
2 CONC rah B. Gober Temple and Kenneth Coleman, GEORGIA JOURNEYS, the ship was named "Georgia Pink" and left on the Thames River in London. Among those passengers were John Graham, his wife, Mary, and children, John, Mary, and Will. This
