1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for SOUTH CAROLINA with the rank of CAPTAIN.   [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A201343  DAR Ancestor # A201343] Capt. in Col. Peter Ho
2 CONC rry's Regiment. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Grahams of Horry" by Harmon Dock Graham retrieved from  http://www.hchsonline.org/Grahams%20of%20Horry%20by%20Harmon%20D.%20Graham.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT The second John Graham (1746-1811) and his wife, Martha, had several children, one of which was Joseph Graham (1790-after 1860), father of Alpha A. Graham (1826-1900). This John Graham served in the Revolutionary War. He was a cap
2 CONC tain in Co. "G" of Colonel Peter Horry's Regiment. There are South Carolina Archive records that show he paid for rations for the troops from January through February 16, 1779. There was another entry that showed he had hired a ca
2 CONC rt and two horses and provided forage for the horses, for the use of the regiment, from January through February 17, 1779. In 1792 he had land granted to him on the south side of Lake Swamp above the mouth of Joyner Swamp. In 1802
2 CONC  he served on the First Board of Commissioners in Conwayborough, South Carolina. In 1804 he sold his land on Mitchell Swamp to his brother, William. After he sold out to William, he moved to the land granted to him in 1792. In 180
2 CONC 5 he served as one of the Justices of the Quorum for the Horry District of South Carolina. He died in 1811 and left his son, Joseph, in charge of his grist mill plantation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Group Sheet
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Graham, Sr., b. About 1746, Horry County, South Carolina. He married Martha, in Horry County, South Carolina, b. Horry County, South Carolina, d. Horry County, South Carolina. John died 1811 , Horry County, South Carolina. Ch
2 CONC ildren: 6. John James Graham b. Abt. 1774. 11 Jennet Graham, b . Horry County, South Carolina. 111 Margaret Graham, b. Horry County, South Carolina. 7. IV William Graham b. 1782 (Cen.1850). 8. V Joseph Graham b. 1790 (Cen.1850). V
2 CONC I Elizabeth Graham, b. Horry County, South Carolina. vn Mary Graham, b.Horry County, South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Bullock is a mystery. Needs more documentation to be labeled a wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1730
2 CONT
2 CONT Stirlingshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT     * The "Ancestry Hints" search engine is combing through the world's largest collection of historical records and family trees to find any possible matches for Margaret Bullock, most matches are junk.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Grahams of Horry" by Harmon Dock Graham retrieved from  http://www.hchsonline.org/Grahams%20of%20Horry%20by%20Harmon%20D.%20Graham.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT John Graham, Sr., b. About 1746, Horry County, South Carolina. He married Martha, in Horry County, South Carolina, b. Horry County, South Carolina, d. Horry County, South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT John died 1811 , Horry County, South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * John James Graham b. Abt. 1774.
2 CONT * Jennet Graham, b . Horry County, South Carolina.
2 CONT * Margaret Graham, b. Horry County, South Carolina.
2 CONT * William Graham b. 1782 (Cen.1850).
2 CONT * Joseph Graham b. 1790 (Cen.1850).
2 CONT * Elizabeth Graham, b. Horry County, South Carolina.
2 CONT * Mary Graham, b.Horry County, South Carolina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT No evidence found for a wife named Margaret. 
