1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gilbert III was born c. 1756 and was the first to spell his surname "Johnston". His wife's name is unknown. Their son was Samuel Johnston, who was born in South Carolina in 1788. At some point, Samuel dropped the "
2 CONC t" in his surname and went by "Johnson". He married Martha "Patsy" Collier (born c. 1805 in TN) on January 13, 1820 in Vicksburg, MS. Land records show that Samuel and Patsy moved from Warren County to Carroll County, MS around 18
2 CONC 35. He died sometime between 1850/1860 and she between 1860/1870. Their children were William, Gilbert (a/k/a Doc), Sarah, Hugh, John, Martha and Samuel Parsons (a/k/a S.P.)
2 CONT
