1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.jamesboswell.info/biography/henrietta-dundas-viscountess-duncan
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrietta Dundas (ca 1748 - 8 December 1832j) was the daughter  of Robert Dundas (1713-1787), sometime Lord President of the Court of Session in Scotland, and Henrietta Carmichael (d. 1755). In 1777 she married Captain (later Admi
2 CONC ral) Adam Duncan (1731-1804), who in the fall of 1797 was made Viscount Duncan of Camperdown and Baron Duncan of Lundie, in recognition of his impressive victory over a Dutch fleet earlier that year.1 The couple had at least four 
2 CONC daughters and two sons, including Robert (1785-1859)2 and Henry (1786-1835).3
2 CONT
2 CONT An obituary in Gentleman's Magazine said of her that "Her many amiable qualities and her fascinating manners will long endear the memory of Lady Duncan. She continued in possession of all her faculties to her advanced age."4
2 CONT
2 CONT She lies buried at the Canongate Churchyard in Edinburgh.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Life with Boswell
2 CONT
2 CONT >Boswell visited Arniston House, the home of the Dundas family, in January 1767. He describes in his journal how he played "Dams with Miss Dundas"5 and that she was a "fine girl. Liked her very well; was retenu for fear of appeari
2 CONC ng lover."6
2 CONT
2 CONT
