1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was educated at Winchester College, Winchester, Hampshire, England.  He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) (Tory) for Warwick between 1802 and 1816.  He held the office of Recorder of Warwick between
2 CONC  1816 and 1835.  He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl Brooke of Warwick Castle [G.B., 1746] on 2 May 1816.  He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Warwick [G.B., 1759] on 2 May 1816.  He succeeded to the title of 10th Baron Bro
2 CONC oke of Beauchamps Court, co. Warwick [E., 1621] on 2 May 1816.  He held the office of Lord-Lieutenant of Warwickshire between 1822 and 1853.  He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Thistle (K.T.) on 10 May 1827.  He held the of
2 CONC fice of Lord of the Bedchamber between 1828 and November 1830.  He was awarded the honorary degree of Doctor of Civil laws (D.C.L.) by Oxford University, Oxford, Oxfordshire, England, on 10 June 1834.  He held the office of Lord-i
2 CONC n-Waiting between 1841 and 1846.
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Peerage
