2 CONT 5a''' Charles MURRAY''' later MURRAY-AYNSLEY (roy licence) (Very Rev); born 21 Oct 1771; Dean Bocking; married 18 June 1793 Alicia (died 18 June 1813), daughter of George Mitford and heiress of her great-uncle Gawen Aynsley, and d
2 CONC ied5 May 1808, 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/24/mode/2up Page 25 - No. 105-g
2 CONT
2 CONT 105(g) '''Charles Murray''', born 21st April 177 1 ; died 5th May 1808. He was Archdeacon of Sodor and Man. On 18th June 1793 he married Alicia, daughter of George Midford, who died 13th June 181 3. Under the Will of a great uncle
2 CONC  she assumed the name of Aynsley, and her husband did likewise. They had issue according to Burke's Peerage:
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2223.htm#i22226
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Very Rev. Lord Charles Murray-Aynsley'''1 M, #22226, b. 21 October 1771, d. 5 May 1808
2 CONT
2 CONT Very Rev. Lord Charles Murray-Aynsley was born on 21 October 1771.1 He was the son of Sir John Murray, 3rd Duke of Atholl and Lady Charlotte Murray, Baroness Strange.1 He married Alicia Mitford, daughter of George Mitford, on 18 J
2 CONC une 1793.1 He died on 5 May 1808 at age 36.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He was given the name of Charles Murray at birth.1 His name was legally changed to Charles Murray-Aynsley.1 He held the office of Dean of Bocking.1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Very Rev. Lord Charles Murray-Aynsley and Alicia Mitford'''
2 CONT * Charlotte Murray-Aynsley1 d. 27 Feb 1827
2 CONT * Atholl Keturah Murray-Aynsley+1 d. 26 Jan 1844
2 CONT * Elizabeth Anne Murray-Aynsley1 d. 7 Jun 1880
2 CONT * John Murray-Aynsley+1 b. 2 Jun 1795, d. Mar 1870
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations===
2 CONT
2 CONT * [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 138. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage,
2 CONC  106th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Very Rev. Lord Charles Murray-Aynsley''' (21 October 1771 – 5 May 1808) was an English dean.
2 CONT
2 CONT Murray-Aynsley was the youngest of nine children of John Murray, 3rd Duke of Atholl, and Charlotte Murray, Duchess of Atholl, and baptized as Charles Murray. On 18 June 1793 he married Alicia Mitford (1768–1813), daughter of Georg
2 CONC e Mitford, and heiress of her great-uncle, Gawen Aynsley, Esq. Upon the marriage, he assumed the surname Aynsley.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1803 Murray-Aynsley was made Dean of Bocking, in Essex, where he entertained King Louis XVIII of France and his suite. The Very Revd Philip Need, Dean of Bocking, described the visit as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Year 1808 the exiled French King Louis 18th, living nearby at Gosfield Hall, was entertained by Dean Charles Murray-Aynsley at Bocking Deanery, all the parish taking part in the fun and celebrations. A job was found for eve
2 CONC ryone in the village so that they could share in the royal celebration. On the day in question it snowed heavily, so some people had the honour of clearing the snow for the King's procession.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Charles and his wife had seven children:
2 CONT * Hon. Charlotte Murray-Aynsley (8 April 1794 – 22 February 1827), married Sir John Oswald on 28 January 1812
2 CONT * Hon. John Murray-Aynsley (2 June 1795 – 25 March 1870), married Emma Sara Peach on 24 June 1820 and had issue, including Hugh Murray-Aynsley.
2 CONT * Hon. Charles Collingwood Murray-Aynsley (1796–1797)
2 CONT * Hon. George Edward Murray-Aynsley (b. 1798), died young
2 CONT * Hon. Athole Keturah Murray-Aynsley (22 July 1801 – 26 January 1844), married Sir Herbert Oakeley, 3rd Baronet on 5 June 1826
2 CONT * Hon. Elizabeth Anne Murray-Aynsley (30 October 1802 – 7 June 1880)
2 CONT * Hon. Charles Edward Murray-Aynsley (December 1805 – August 1815)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lord_Charles_Murray-Aynsley
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
