1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patrick Stuart was a decendant of the Royal house of Scotland. He received a commision as an officer in the Imperial Austrian Army. He became a Generalmajor the 10th of April 1783 and was promoted to Feldmarchalleu
2 CONC tnant 1790
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the Colonel-Propriator of the 18th Line Infantry Regiment from 27th of December 1791 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Graf Patrick Stuart was fighting during 1799 in Italy and on the 18th of September he faught at the battle of Savigliano with his Ist and IIIrd  Battalion. Total manpower of 2363 soldiers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Line Infantry Regiment ‘Furst Reuss zu Greiz’ Nr. 18 (German)
2 CONT
2 CONT Regimental Designations and Colonels-in-Chief:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1791-1799: Infantry Regiment ‘Graf Stuart’ Nr. 18 (Stuart, Feldmarschalleutnant Patrick, Graf) 1809-1809: Infantry Regiment ‘Graf d’Aspre’ Nr. 18 (Aspre von Hoobruck, Feldmarschalleutnant Karl, Graf d’) 1809-1817: Infantry Regimen
2 CONC t ‘Prinz Reuss zu Greiz’ (Reuss zu Greiz, Feldmarschalleutnant Heinrich XIII, Furst) [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonels:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1799-1801: Weber von Treuenfels, Oberst Franz. 1801-1809: Oberdorf, OB Freiherr von 1809-1813: Grimmer von Riesenburg, OB 1813-1815: Georgy, OB Chevalier
2 CONT
2 CONT Subordinate Officers (1799):
2 CONT
2 CONT Dworzeck, Oberstleutnant Anton Grill, Oberstleutnant Josef Weber von Treuenfels, Major Xavier Pruckl, Major
