2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Caroline Stanhope 1765 8 Oct — Age: 21<br/>
2 CONT St. Martin-in-the-Fields, Westminster, Middlesex, England<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Mackenzie married first Lady Caroline Stanhope (1747–1767), daughter of William Stanhope, 2nd Earl of Harrington Title 1766 — Age: 22<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Mackenzie was created Viscount Fortrose and Baron Ardelve in the Peerage of Ireland on 18 November 1766<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation 1768 — Age: 24 He was a Member of Parliament for Buteshire and Caithness from 1768 to 1774<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Title 1771 3 Dec — Age: 27<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT December 1771, he was created Earl of Seaforth (a new peerage, also in the Peerage of Ireland). Occupation<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 1772 12 Nov — Age: 28<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Mackenzie was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society Military<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 1778 — Age: 34 He was commissioned lieutenant-colonel and raised a regiment, the Seaforth (Highland) Regiment in 1778 Military<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 1778 — Age: 34 Kenneth raised the regiment of Highlanders, the 78th (later known as 72nd) in 1778, known later as the 1st battalion of the Seaforth Highlanders.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Death 1781 27 Aug — Age: 37 At sea He died in August 1781 at age 37, without male issue.On his death, his titles became extinct<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Title 1781 — Age: 37 Kenneth Mackenzie was created Earl of Seaforth in 1771, but his peerage became extinct when he died in August 1781. Although there were still heirs to the older earldom, this remained under attainder<br/>
2 CONT
