1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir William Forbes, 6th Baronet</strong> (5 April 1739 – 12 November 1806) was a Scottish banker, born in Edinburgh to Sir William Forbes, 5th Baronet, and Christian Forbes. On 20 September 1770 he married Elizabeth Hay (
2 CONC died 26 December 1789), daughter of Sir James Hay of Haystoun, 4th Baronet of Smithfield and Dorriel Campbell. They had six children:
2 CONT * Sir William Forbes, 7th Baronet of Pitsligo (21 December 1773 – 10 October 1828)
2 CONT * John Hay Forbes of Medwyn (September 1776–1854)
2 CONT * Christian Forbes
2 CONT * Rebecca Forbes, who married in 1802 Alexander Ranaldson MacDonell of Glengarry
2 CONT * Elizabeth Forbes
2 CONT * Jane Forbes
2 CONT
2 CONT He became partner in the banking firm of Messrs. John Coutts & Co.; two years later a new company was formed, of which he rose to be manager, and which in 1830 became the Union Bank of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was author of a <em>Life of his friend Beattie</em>, the Scottish poet, and of <em>Memoirs of a Banking-House</em>."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Sir William Forbes, 6th Baronet', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 30 November 2012, 22:09 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sir_William_Forbes,_6th_Baronet&oldid=525766524
2 CONC > [accessed 5 December 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n323/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 305-306
2 CONT *[http://www.bbc.co.uk/arts/yourpaintings/paintings/william-forbes-of-pitsligo-17391806-85778 BBC - Your Paintings - William Forbes of Pitsligo (1739–1806)]
1 FAMC @F6000000008994163355@
