1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fairfield District, South Carolina Wills, Vol 1, book 5, page 80, March 1804. Lists wife Margaret, children David, Margaret, Elizabeth, Hugh and Jane. Son James (if related) would have been 63 years old living in C
2 CONC leveland or Chester District. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Per publication by Gina Bell, son James came from Northern Ireland to Charleston, South Carolina in 1773 with brothers Charles, David, and Hugh and sisters Jane, Margaret, and Nancy. Sister Martha came by way of Wilmington, North 
2 CONC Carolina in 1775. Order of birth and parents names were not noted. RELATIONSHIP INFO NOT PROVEN.
2 CONT
2 CONT This taken from Mel Stephens notes sent in a Gedcom file via email January 13, 2000. His email address is melstephens@sprintmail.com
2 CONT
2 CONT In a later email from Mel dated May 16, 2000, he told me he thinks this Hugh might possibly have been a brother to James instead of James' father. He thinks this family that came to South Carolina in 1773 came after their father d
2 CONC ied, possibly with what inheritance they might have received. The fact that Martha came two years later suggests to Mel that she might have stayed behind to care for their mother
