1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "Mr Falconer of Monktown, the father of Lady Colquhoun, was son of Patrick Falconer, who was son of Sir James Falconer, a Lord of Session, as Lord Phesdo, and Dame Elizabeth Trent, his spouse. Lord Phesdo was a son of Sir John Fal
2 CONC coner, Master of the Mint to King Charles the Second. Sir John was a younger brother of the first Lord Falconer of Haulkerton. The mother of Lady Colquhoun was also of the same family, being the Honourable Jean Falconer, eldest da
2 CONC ughter of David Lord Falconer of Haulkerton."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/n433/mode/2up The chiefs of Colquhoun and their country], by William Fraser, 1869, page 385
