1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir David Dalrymple, 3rd Baronet, Lord Hailes</strong> (October 28, 1726 – November 29, 1792) was a Scottish advocate, judge and historian, born in Edinburgh...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...His father, Sir James Dalrymple, 2nd Baronet, of Hailes, Haddingtonshire, Auditor of the Exchequer in Scotland, was a grandson of James Dalrymple, 1st Viscount of Stair; and his mother, Lady Christian Hamilton, was a daughter o
2 CONC f Thomas Hamilton, 6th Earl of Haddington. The eldest of sixteen children, he succeeded to his father's baronetcy upon his death in 1751...
2 CONT
2 CONT He was twice married: (1) in 1763, to Anne, daughter of Sir George Broun, Lord Coalston, a Lord of Session, by whom he had a daughter, Christian (d.1838). He remarried (2) March 20, 1770, Helen (d. 1799), daughter of Sir James Fer
2 CONC gusson, Baronet, of Kilkerran, Ayrshire, by whom he had another daughter, Jean (d.1803) who married her cousin, James Fergusson, Esq., and left issue."
2 CONT
