1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Philip Anstruther-Paterson, Baronet [S. 1700], of Anstruther and Elie House</strong>, formerly Philip Anstruther, 1st s. and h., b. 13 Jan. 1752, at Edinburgh ; sometime Lieutenant 1st Dragoon Guards ; M.P. for Anstru
2 CONC ther Easter burghs, 1774, till he resigned in 1777 ; took the name of Paterson after that of Anstruther about 1782, in consequence of his marriage ; suc. to the Baronetcy, 4 July 1799. He m. 19 Feb. 1778, at Eccles, co. Berwick, A
2 CONC nne, da. and h. of Sir John Paterson, 3d Baronet [S. 1687], of Eccles aforesaid, by Anne, de jure (10 Jan. 1794), sou jure Baroness Polwarth [S.], 1st da. and heir of line of Hugh (Hume-Campbell), 3d Earl of Marchmont and Lord Pol
2 CONC warth [S.]. He d. s.p., 5 Jan. 1808, aged about 56 the estate of Eccles having already been sold. His widow, who in 1818, claimed the Barony of Polwarth [S.], d. s.p. 11 March 1822. Will pr. 1822."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n405/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 387-388
2 CONT
