2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Anstruther, Baronet [S. 1700 and G.B. 1798], of Anstruther and Elie House</strong>, br. and h., b. at Elie House, 27 March 1753; admitted to Lincoln's Inn, 12 Feb. 1774; Advocate, 30 July 1774 ; Barrister (Lincol
2 CONC n's Inn), 1779 ; M.P. for Anstruther Easter Burghs (two Paris.), 1783-90; for Cockermouth, 1790-96, and for Anstruther Easter Burghs (again), 1796-97, and 1806 till death, taking a leading part in the impeachment of Warren Hasting
2 CONC s ; was Chief Justice of the Supreme Court at Bengal, 1796-1806 ; Knighted,4, Oct. 1797, and was cr. a Baronet [G.B.], 18 May 1798, as "of Port William, Bengal"; P.C., 19 Nov. 1806; suc. to the Baronetcy [S. 1700], 5 Jan. 1808, an
2 CONC d was, 14 March 1808, served heir of entail to his br., the late Baronet. He was cr. D.C.L. of the Univ. of Oxford, 3 July 1810. He m. in or before 1784, Maria Isabella, 1st da. of Edward Brice, of Berners street, Marylebone. He d
2 CONC . 26 Jan. 1811, in Albemarle Street, aged 57. Will pr. 1811. His widow d. 14 June 1833, in Conduit street. Will pr. July 1833."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n407/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 388
2 CONT
