1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JANET CLERK (aka JENNY CLERK) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Clerk, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-John-Clerk-of-Penicuik-2nd-baronet/6000000004172539543?through=6000000011026356483 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Clerk/6000000004172
2 CONC 674074?through=6000000011026356483 She was born before 17 August 1727, the date upon which hr baptism was registered at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Baptisms, reference OPR.697/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Clerk, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/James-Carmichael-of-Hailes-WS/6000000017624050042?through=6000000011026356483 Their ante-nuptial marriage contract was signed on 16 April 1750. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f1881&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Clerk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1800&di=n NRS: GD18/1881]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                      1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 April 1750: Ante-nuptial Marriage Contract between James Carmichaell, Clerk to the Signet, second son of William Carmichaell [Carmichael] of Skirling, advocate, and Janet Clerk, sixth daughter of Sir John Clerk of Pennycook 
2 CONC [Penicuik], bt. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f1881&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Clerk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1800&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk family o
2 CONC f Penicuik, Midlothian, reference GD18/1881]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1750-51: Letters to Sir John Clerk and George Clerk regarding the marriage of Janet Clerk, daughter of Sir John, to James Carmichael, son of William Carmichael of Skirling. Writers are said to be Sir John and William and James 
2 CONC Carmichael. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f5476&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Janet+Clerk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1800&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk family of Pe
2 CONC nicuik, Midlothian, reference GD18/5476]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                            3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 December 1783: Copy Assignation by Janet Clerk, relict of James Carmichael of Hailes, to her brother, John Clerk of Eldin, of all her means and estate at her decease, on payment of her debts and the legacies specified. [http
2 CONC s://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f1997&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=James+Carmichael+of+Hailes&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk family of Penicuik
2 CONC , Midlothian, reference GD18/1997]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary for her Husband ==
2 CONT
2 CONT "<strong>Carmichael, James, of Hailes— Apprentice to Hugh Somerville. — Second son of the Hon. William Carmichael of Skirling, Advocate. Died 12th January 1781. Mar. 16th April 1750, Jenny, youngest daughter of Sir John Clerk of P
2 CONC enicuik, Bart. [https://archive.org/details/historyofsociety00socirich/page/35/mode/1up A History of the Society of Writers to Her Majesty's Signet, etc. (Edinburgh, 1890), p. 35]'''
