1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Alexander Gilmour, Baronet [S. 1678], of Craigmiller</strong>, only s. and h. ; b. probably about 1735; suc. to the Baronetcy, 9 Aug. 1750, and had service to his father, 4 April 1752. In 1754 he claimed, unsuccessful
2 CONC ly, the estate of Balnagowan on the death of his cousin William (Ross), 14th and last Lord Ross of Halkhead [S.]. He was an officer in the Foot Guards ; was one of the Clerk Comptrollers of the Board of Green Cloth, 1765 ; M.P. fo
2 CONC r co Edinburgh (three Paris.), 1761-74. He m. [— ]. She d. Jan. 1780. He d. s.p. in France, 27 Dec. 1792, when the Baronetcy became extinct."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n325/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 306
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1754-1790/member/gilmour-sir-alexander-1737-92 The History of Parliament: the House of Commons 1754-1790], ed. L. Namier, J. Brooke., 1964
