2 CONT The Life Summary of Robert Alexander
2 CONT When Robert Alexander Askey was born in 1768, in Fannett Township, Franklin, Pennsylvania, United States, his father, Thomas Erskine Askey, was 41 and his mother, Elizabeth "Betsy" Baker, was 23. He married Mary Elizabeth Polly Ev
2 CONC ans on 5 December 1801, in Chestnut Ridge, Redstone Township, Fayette, Pennsylvania, United States. They were the parents of at least 6 sons and 6 daughters. He died on 16 April 1850, in Pike Township, Clearfield, Pennsylvania, Un
2 CONC ited States, at the age of 82, and was buried in McClure Cemetery, Pike Township, Clearfield, Pennsylvania, United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Pike Township, Clearfield, Pennsylvania, United States - 1850
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Robert fought in the Indian Wars in Ohio and in the War of 1812. He was given 400 acres in Clearfield County on a Land Grant.
