1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel, is quite likely his most colorful ancestor and rivals Thomas for his many contributions to the Askey story. Samuel was a frontiersman and mountain man in Pennsylvania who was well known for his hunting skil
2 CONC ls and his many close calls encountering mountain lions, bears and other animals. He enjoyed a reputation as a woodsman that, according to some, rivaled Daniel Boone and Davy Crockett. He also served with future President, William
2 CONC  Henry Harrison, during the war of 1812 at the battle of Lake Erie. Samuel was the eighth child among the ten born to Thomas and Betsy. He married Mary Letitia McKibbin in 1803 and they had 14 children together. 
2 CONT
