1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT Claimant of the compensation as legatee and appointee of Lady Mary Walker for the enslaved people on the Success estate in St James, the compensation for which was paid into a Chancery suit.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter and residuary heiress of Lady Mary Walker, otherwise Hamilton: her father was probably George Robert Hamilton of Jamaica. Burial of Sophia St John Alderson aged 73 of Regent Place, Regents Square at All Souls Kensal Green
2 CONC  10/05/1856
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ucl.ac.uk/lbs/person/view/12004
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/ugo-foscolo_%28Enciclopedia-Italiana%29/
2 CONT The rest of his military life, which lasted until the fall of the Italian Kingdom, is of no particular importance: indeed, when he was in France, from June 1804 to March 1806, with the Italian division that had come to increase th
2 CONC e great army that Napoleon was gathering on the banks of the Channel against his rival England, he was assigned to sedentary services, very unwelcome to him, in the various garrisons of Valenciennes, Calais,Lille, Boulogne-sur -We
2 CONC d; and then, having returned to Italy, he nevertheless remained an official, although he frequently regretted not obtaining that rank to which he aspired by full right, but it does not seem that he ever had such precise obligation
2 CONC s as to have to neglect his beloved literary studies and the beloved art.
2 CONT
2 CONT To whom and to which the many, too many loves, always vehement and passionate, often desperate and frantic, which he nurtured, in the period we are now dealing with, for an overwhelming number of women or young girls, maidens or b
2 CONC rides: for Teresa Pichler Monti; for Isabella Roncioni; for Antonietta Fagnani Arese; for Fanny Emerytt; for Marzia Martinengo; for Francesca Giovio; for Maddalena Bignami; for Lucietta Battaglia; for Cornelia Rossi Martinetti; fo
2 CONC r Eleonora Nencini; for Quirina Mocenni Magiotti; for still others.
