2 CONT "<strong>Sir James Erskine, Baronet [1791], of Torrie</strong>, br. and h. ; b. 30 Sep. 1772, entered the 26th Foot in 1788, and served as Captain of Dragoons in Flanders and as Aide-de-Camp to General Vyse, 1793-94; was promoted 
2 CONC as Major for his conduct at the battle of Catean, 26 April 1794, and was, as Lieut.-Col. of the 15th Light Dragoons, at the battle of Bergen, 2 Oct. 1799; Aide-de-Camp to the King, 1800 ; Lieut.-Col. 2d Dragoon Guards, 1803, and, 
2 CONC finally, Major-Gen. in the Army, 1808. He suc. to the Baronetcy, 13 Feb. 1813. He m. 5 March 1801, Louisa, sister to the 1st Marqdess of Angeksey, 3d. da. of Henry (Paget) 1st Eart. of Uxbridge, by Jane, da. of the Very Rev. Arthu
2 CONC r Champagne, Dean of Clonmacnoise. He d. s.p., in Dover street, Piccadilly, 3 March 1825, aged 52. Will pr. April 1825. His widow, who was 6. 26 March 1777, m. in 1826, General the Right Hon. Sir George Murray, Gr.C.B. (who d. 28 
2 CONC July 1846, aged 74), and d. 23 Jan. 1842, in Belgrave square, in her 65th year."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524416#page/n291/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1906; Vol. V; page 269
