1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Wikipedia contributors. "<em>[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Haldane James Haldane]</em>." Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia.
2 CONT * Burke, Bernard, Sir.  [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera01byuburk#page/708/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry of Great Britain & Ireland 6th ed]. London : Harrison 1879. Vol I. page 708
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Was brought up in the care of his grandmother, Lady Lundie, and his uncles. Dundee grammar school and high school in Edinburgh, entered Edinburgh University in 1781, attending art classes. In 1785 he became a midshipman on board t
2 CONC he Duke of Montrose, East Indiaman and made four voyages to India and China, becoming second officer. In 1794 he settled in Edinburgh. With Charles Simeon of Cambridge he made an evangelistic tour of Scotland in 1797, from which C
2 CONC ongregational Churches developed. His last 57 year were gratuitously dedicated to the cause of Christ by his preaching, his itineraries and his writing. Along with his brother Robert, he was instrumental in promoting a remarkable 
2 CONC revival of religion in Scotland. For 50 years he was the devoted pastor of the Tabernacle Church, Edinburgh, and was honoured to win many souls to Christ.
