1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was the son of Admiral Adam Duncan, 1st Viscount Duncan of Camperdown and Henrietta Dundas.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was baptised with the name of Robert Dundas Duncan.
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the rank of Ensign in 1797 in the service of the Coldstream Guards.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 2nd Viscount Duncan of Camperdown [G.B., 1797] on 4 August 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded to the title of 2nd Baron Duncan of Lundie, co. Perth [G.B., 1797] on 4 August 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Grand Master of the Freemasons [Scotland] between 1812 and 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Earl of Camperdown of Lundie, co. Forfar and of Gleneagles, co. Perth [U.K.] on 12 September 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Thistle (K.T.) on 12 May 1848.
