2 CONT
2 CONT that on 18 May 1854 John Peter Carruthers-Wade, the only son of John Peter Wade and his wife Rachel, daughter and heiress of John Carruthers of Holmains and Kirkwood (died 1809), in obedience to a Deed of Entail executed by his au
2 CONC nt, ''Mrs Elizabeth Maria Carruthers'' of Holmains, sister of the petitioner’s mother, recorded in the Public Register (Volume 5 Folio 53) the Arms of Carruthers of Holmains quarterly, second and third, with the Arms of Wade; [htt
2 CONC ps://www.trove.scot/place/259015 Holmains, Dalton, Dumfries And Galloway 55.07500, -3.43833]
2 CONT
2 CONT that Peter John Carruthers-Wade died without issue on 1 March 1873, when the succession opened to his nephew, William Mitchell-Carruthers, grandson of Susan Carruthers of Holmains, sister of the said Rachel and Elizabeth Maria Car
2 CONC ruthers of Holmains;
