2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://doverhistorian.com/2013/12/24/dynasty-of-dover-part-iv-minet-fector/ Dynasty of Dover Part IV – Minet-Fector by Lorraine]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT John Minet Fector married Anne Wortley Montague Laurie (1769-1848) of Glencairn, Dumfries, in 1794. She was the daughter of General Sir Robert Laurie, member of Parliament for the county of Dumfries. They had four children, Anne J
2 CONC udith Fector born 1799, Charlotte Mary Fector born 1801, Caroline Fector born 1804 and John Minet Fector junior born 28 March 1812. James married Frances Lane, daughter of Thomas Bateman Lane in November 1783 and had five children
2 CONC , three of which survive to adulthood. They were, Peter Lane born 1787, Mary born 1791 and Emma born 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10150-4787876/ann-fector-in-1841-england-wales-census MyHeritage: Ann Fector: 1841 England & Wales Census]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 June 1841 Census for residents of [https://maps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=19.2&lat=51.12822&lon=1.31746&layers=117746211&b=1&marker=51.128092,1.317042 Laureston House, now 9 Laureston Place, Dover, Kent CT16 1QX 51.128092, 1.3170
2 CONC 42], England
2 CONT * Ann Fector, head (implied), female, aged 70 - 74 [born between 1767 and 1771], in Scotland
2 CONT * Ann Hughes, female, aged 40 - 44 [born between 1797 and 1801], in Out of County; Female servant
2 CONT * Ellen Marsh, female, aged 45 - 49 [born between 1792 and 1796], in Kent, England; Female servant
2 CONT * Ann Boston, female, aged 30 - 34 [born between 1807 and 1811], in Kent, England; Female servant
2 CONT * Joseph Lucker, male, aged 40 - 44 [born between 1797 and 1801], in Out of County; Male servant
2 CONT * Francis Leath, male, aged 25 - 29 [born between 1812 and 1816], in Kent, England; Male servant
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=PCm60xSAXnr9cy%2B43McdnA&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of death of Anne Wortley Montague Fector in 1848]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT January to March 1848: Registration of death of Anne Wortley Montague Fector; [no age given]; in St Pancras (Volume 1, Page 312)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0003089/18480401/033/0003 British Newspaper Archive: Glasgow Courier Saturday, 1 April 1848 Page 3 Deaths]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Deaths: On Sunday, 26 March 1848 [ultimo], Anne Wortley Montague Fector, widow of the late J. M. Fector, Esq., and only daughter of the late Lieutenant General Sir Robert Laurie, Bart., M.P. for Dumfriesshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000235/18480404/059/0003 British Newspaper Archive: Kentish Gazette Tuesday, 4 April 1848 Page 3 Deaths]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Deaths: Fector. — Sunday, 26 March 1848, at Regent's Park, Mrs. Fector, relict of J. M. Fector, Esq., of Dover, aged 77.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000235/18480404/036/0003 British Newspaper Archive: Kentish Gazette Tuesday, 4 April 1848 Page 3 Dover, April 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT At noon today, Tuesday, 4 April 1848, the funeral of Mrs. A. U. M. Fector (the widow of the late J. M. Fector, Esq. banker), who died on Sunday, 26 March 1848 [ultimo] in London), took place in St. James's churchyard.  [https://ma
2 CONC ps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=19.3&lat=51.12626&lon=1.31839&layers=117746211&b=1&marker=51.126160,1.318538 St James's Church Burial Ground, now Woolcomber Street Car Park, 2 Castle Hill Road, Dover, Kent CT16 1QN 51.126160, 1.318538
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT The remains of the deceased lady were conducted from London to the terminus of the South-Eastern Railway by Mr. W. H. Stone, of the Apollonian Hall, formerly butler to the deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral cortège consisted of a hearse and two mourning coaches, each drawn by four horses, with plumes and mutes, and were followed to their last resting place by her son, J. M. Fector, Esq., late M.P. for Maidstone, her son-i
2 CONC n-law, Sir John Bayley, Bart., and her relatives, Colonel Matson, R.E., Captain Dickenson, and their respective sons. Upon the arrival of the corpse at Saint James's church, it was placed in the centre aisle, and thence removed to
2 CONC  the family vault in the burial ground, the service being performed by the Rev. Mr. Darwall. 
2 CONT
2 CONT An immense assemblage of persons followed the deceased to the ground out of respect to her, and the tradesmen's shops in the line of the procession were pretty generally closed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The age of deceased was 77 and she survived her brother the late Admiral Sir Robert Laurie, about two months.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://discovery.nationalarchives.gov.uk/details/r/D124558 The National Archives: Will of Anne Wortley Montague Fector, Widow of River, Kent]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: PROB 11/2074/261
2 CONT * Description: Will of Anne Wortley Montague Fector, Widow, of River, Kent
2 CONT * Date: Monday, 1 May 1848
2 CONT * Held by: The National Archives, Kew
2 CONT * Legal status: Public Record(s)
2 CONT * Closure status: Open Document, Open Description
