2 CONC 1869 Page 23]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald Alison. D.C.L., F.R.S., an eminent lawyer and historian, author of a standard book on the Criminal Law, and of a very celebrated History of Europe, and other works; was born at Kinley, Salop, Saturday, 29 December 1792. 
2 CONC He was created a baronet, Friday, 25 June 1852; he was sheriff of Lanarkshire; he married Monday, 21 March 1825, Elizabeth Glencairn Tytler, youngest daughter of Lieutenant Colonel Patrick Tytler. late assistant quartermaster-gene
2 CONC ral in Scotland, by his wife, Isabella Erskine, daughter of the Hon. James Erskine, Lord Alva, one of the senators of the College of Justice, a lineal descendant of the families of the Duke of Lennox, a branch of the royal Stuart 
2 CONC family and Earls of March and had issue...
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieutenant Colonel Patrick Tytler was second son of William Tytler, Esq. of Woodhouselee, younger brother of Alexander Fraser Tytler, Lord Woodhouselee, a senator of the college of justice, and uncle of Patrick Fraser Tytler, the 
2 CONC historian of Scotland.
2 CONT
