2 DATE 1 AUG 1869
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Hamilton_(bishop) Walter Kerr Hamilton] was the Anglican Bishop of Salisbury from 27 March 1854 to 1 August 1869.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 1808, educated at Eton College, tutored by Thomas Arnold, and then attended Christ Church College, University of Oxford, where he took a first class degree in Greats. He was elected to a Fellowship at Merton College
2 CONC  in 1832. He was made deacon in 1833 and ordained priest in December of the same year. He was a curate at Wolvercote and at the parish of S. Peter-in-the-East in Oxford. He became vicar of that parish in 1837 where he remained unt
2 CONC il 1841. He subsequently became a canon-resident of Salisbury and then bishop of said Diocese in 1854.
2 CONT
2 CONT His private papers are currently in the possession of the Archives of Pusey House, Oxford.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Walter Hamilton (bishop)', Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, 22 September 2013, 10:49 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Walter_Hamilton_(bishop)&oldid=574029746> [accessed 24 Novembe
2 CONC r 2013]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Hamilton_(bishop)
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter Kerr Hamilton was a Church of England priest, Bishop of Salisbury from 27 March 1854 to 1 August 1869.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born in 1808, educated at Eton College, tutored by Thomas Arnold, and then attended Christ Church, University of Oxford, where he took a first class degree in Greats. He was elected to a Fellowship at Merton College in 1832
2 CONC . He was made deacon in 1833 and ordained priest in December of the same year. He was a curate at Wolvercote and at the parish of S. Peter-in-the-East in Oxford. He became vicar of that parish in 1837 where he remained until 1841.
2 CONC  He subsequently became a canon-resident of Salisbury and then bishop of said Diocese in 1854.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Isabel Elizabeth Lear. His daughter, Eleanor Frances Hamilton, married Dr. Ernest Kingscote (b. 9 Sep 1856, d. 16 Jun 1934) in 1887.
2 CONT
2 CONT His private papers are currently in the possession of the Archives of Pusey House, Oxford.
