1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Alexander Lockhart of Covington</strong> - Son of George Lockhart of Carnwarth, and Lady Euphemia Montgomery, daughter of the Earl of Eglinton, passed as advocate 20th January 1722...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...After practising as an advocate for upwards of half a century, he was appointed successor to Alexander Fraser of Strichen, and took his seat by the title of <strong>Lord Covington</strong>, on the 10th March 1775, and died on t
2 CONC he 10th November 1782, in the eighty-second year of his age."
2 CONT
