0 @N6000000006127800203@ NOTE Kenneth, third Lord Duffus, succeeded his father James in 1705. As a captain in the Queen's Navy (Queen Anne.1702-14), he, in 1711 with his frigate of forty-six guns, engaged eight French privateers, and wounded by five bullets wa
1 CONC s captured.Although he voted for the Union of the English and Scottish Parliaments (1707), he joined the Jacobites in 1715, leading that year more than four hundred of the rebels into Tain and there proclaimed the Chevalier St. Ge
1 CONC orge, 'The Old Pretender' asKing James VIII. The Lairds of Culloden and Kilravock refusing to surrender, the rebels marched South to join the Earl of Mar at Perth. After the Jacobite defeat of 171S the estate of Duffus was forfeit
1 CONC ed and Lord Duffus, by way of Caithness,escaped to Sweden. Preparing to return to Britain he was seized in Hamburg and imprisoned in the Tower of London but freed without trial in 1717. Later he entered the Russian Navy. He marrie
1 CONC d (contract dated 1708) Charlotta Chnstina, daughter ofEric Sioblade, Governor of Gottenberg in Sweden. He died in or before 1734 and had one son and two daughters: 
